WEBVTT

1
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:09,400
[mysterious atmospheric music playing]

2
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,480
[woman panting]

3
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,040
[music becomes suspenseful]

4
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:05,800
[silence falls]

5
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,800
[eerie piano music rises]

6
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:16,280
THE SECRET WOMAN

7
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:24,320
2 YEARS LATER

8
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:36,520
[bells tolling]

9
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,960
BASED ON ANNA EKBERG'SDEN
<i>HEMMELIGE KVINDE</i>

10
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,240
[music becomes gentle]

11
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:27,200
[man] Have you checked the nets yet? Good.

12
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:29,880
-[woman] Hi!
-[man] Ah, it's the Danish girl.

13
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,440
[boy] Morning, Louise.

14
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:34,960
-Here you go.
-[gasps] Wow!

15
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:35,880
Lovely.

16
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:37,880
Wow.

17
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,000
Tell me, how's your mum?

18
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,600
-Better.
-Yeah?

19
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:46,200
Well, as soon as she's well enough,
come for some hot chocolate at the café.

20
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,840
-Okay?
-Okay.

21
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:50,240
[both chuckling]

22
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,080
[mysterious music playing]

23
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:55,640
Balder?

24
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:57,360
-Eight hundred kroner?
-Yep.

25
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,800
-[Louise] Say hi to your mum.
-[boy] Sure.

26
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:02,000
[Balder] See you soon.

27
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,640
[gentle music playing]

28
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:09,680
-[Louise] Morning.
-Hi.

29
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,680
[straining] Oi.

30
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,320
All right, what do we have here?

31
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,640
[gasps] Oh, perfect!

32
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:19,440
-Huh?
-Oh, lovely!

33
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:22,040
-[laughs] Let's put crab on our specials.
-Uh-huh.

34
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,600
-Okay. Thanks.
-I'll put them in the kitchen.

35
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:37,440
CRIME SCENE DO NOT CROSS
SERIAL KILLERS

36
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,880
A COMPLETE GUIDE
TO POLICE PROCEDURE

37
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:04,440
[Louise] Hmm.

38
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,320
[Louise] Good morning.

39
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,440
-Hi.
-Late night?

40
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,880
[breathy chuckle]

41
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:12,240
Did I wake you?

42
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,960
-No. No, not at all.
-Are you sure?

43
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:15,920
Mm.

44
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,920
Get any writing done?
Or did you get distracted?

45
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,120
[chuckles] I don't know what to say.

46
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:21,520
-The pyramids again?
-No.

47
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,760
-No? [chuckles]
-[chuckles]

48
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,280
It was worse than that, in fact.

49
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:28,360
I went down a… a rabbit hole
with Mount Kailash, right.

50
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:31,040
It's a sacred mountain in Tibet actually.

51
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,960
-Mm-hmm.
-There are lots of stories…

52
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:36,040
about all these
temporal distortion things.

53
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:39,040
-[laughs] I love you, you nerd!
-There's more to it.

54
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:41,440
-[laughs] Mm.
-There are conspiracy theories…

55
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:43,520
-[man] Seriously.
-[foghorn blaring]

56
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:46,200
[tour guide] We're now arriving
at the island of Tysnes.

57
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:50,600
A small island
with only 2,400 inhabitants,

58
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:54,480
but one with deep roots in Norse history.

59
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,480
Around the island you will find sites

60
00:04:56,560 --> 00:05:00,160
of great cultural
and historical importance.

61
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:03,320
[camera shutter clicking]

62
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,880
[Louise] Let me know
if you need anything. [chuckles]

63
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:13,960
Thank you, Maria.

64
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:16,320
-You're welcome. Say hi to your folks.
-Yeah, I will.

65
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:17,560
-See you.
-[boy] Bye.

66
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,000
[Louise chuckles]

67
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:20,880
-[Maria] Louise?
-Mm?

68
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:23,720
That guy sitting there
won't stop staring at you.

69
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,720
But you are gorgeous,
so I don't blame him.

70
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,400
[both chuckle]

71
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:28,920
Ooh, well he's coming over here.

72
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,280
-Oh, great.
-Mm.

73
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,040
Helene?

74
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:35,120
It's me, Peter.

75
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:36,920
We, uh, worked at the same company.

76
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,360
Uh, sorry, but I'm not Helene.

77
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:43,840
-Hmm… What do you mean?
-[Louise] My name's Louise.

78
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,240
This is me.

79
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,120
Louise Andersen.

80
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:53,080
-My apologies.
-No worries at all.

81
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,920
[Peter] You must have a doppelgänger.

82
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:04,440
[woman] Congratulations
to Joachim and Louise. Cheers.

83
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:07,120
Here we go. Dinner's served!

84
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,480
-[man] Ooh.
-[Maria] Enjoy.

85
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,840
[glass clinking for attention]

86
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:13,080
[chuckles] Time for me
to make a speech, I'm afraid.

87
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,800
Okay. Um, yeah.

88
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:18,720
We are engaged. She said yes.

89
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:22,680
I'm pleased to say, finally.
Um, it's a very cheap ring, I'm afraid.

90
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:24,160
[group chuckling]

91
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,920
[man] We've been here
almost two years now.

92
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:32,160
And I've never felt more at home as,
um, I do here with you.

93
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,680
Aw, you're welcome.

94
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,760
[man] Thank you.

95
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:36,760
Um, Louise…

96
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:41,040
Um, you are a magical person.

97
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:45,800
-Mysterious. And magical.
-[all chuckling]

98
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:51,960
And I feel like I've spent
a lot of time thinking about all of my…

99
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:54,080
silly, uh, little books

100
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:57,320
and the never-ending mountain
of boring research. Uh…

101
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,240
[all chuckling]

102
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,000
As if that was all that mattered.

103
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,720
But not any more.

104
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:05,200
You bring meaning to my life.

105
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:07,160
Every day.

106
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:10,040
And I adore you.

107
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,360
I love you.

108
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,440
[group cheering]

109
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:24,440
Right, time for you to raise your glass.
To both of you, and love.

110
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:25,520
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

111
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,520
-[woman] Cheers, everyone!
-[door knocking]

112
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,520
[crockery clinking]

113
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:33,680
-[man] Who is it?
-Him again?

114
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:35,840
Who?

115
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:39,440
Uh, there was a Danish man at the café
who wouldn't stop staring at Louise today.

116
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:42,600
He thought I was someone he knew, but…

117
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,880
Oh, yeah?

118
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,880
I'd rather not talk to him again.

119
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:49,560
I'll make sure he gets the message.
[clears throat]

120
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:55,360
[man] Yes?

121
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:57,480
Hi. I'd like to speak to Helene.

122
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:00,560
Yeah, well, sorry, there's no one
called Helene here, I'm afraid.

123
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:04,200
[Peter] Look, I have something
very important to tell her.

124
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,520
It's about her past, okay?

125
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,240
[mysterious music playing]

126
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:10,840
As I said you're, uh…

127
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:13,880
You're barking up the wrong tree,
I would say. So…

128
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:18,440
Okay.

129
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:28,120
He was obnoxious.

130
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:30,640
-[Louise] Yes.
-And you've never seen the guy before?

131
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:33,560
[inhales] I don't think. Um…

132
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:38,760
I don't remember seeing him before, um…
I don't think so, but, erm…

133
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:41,480
Hey. What is it?

134
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:44,440
Is there something
that's coming back to you?

135
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:46,240
Nothing, he just made me…

136
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,480
[inhales deeply]

137
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:50,680
…scared.

138
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,680
[emotional string music playing]

139
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:58,960
[man] Louise, If he's somehow managed
to jog your memory…

140
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:04,920
If you're starting to remember…
you can tell me. We'll figure things out.

141
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,520
Yeah.

142
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:11,800
Thank you.

143
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,240
-Let's sleep now.
-Mm.

144
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:31,080
[thunder rumbling]

145
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,120
[mysterious music playing]

146
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:45,200
[rain pattering]

147
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:20,400
[thunder rumbling]

148
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:26,080
[distorted twinkling]

149
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:30,640
[child] Wow.

150
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
[mysterious music ticking]

151
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:55,400
I'VE GONE TO THE MAINLAND. I'LL BE BACK
ON THE LAST FERRY THIS AFTERNOON.

152
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:56,880
I LOVE YOU!

153
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:09,160
[policewoman] <i>Okay, Louise. You've come</i>
<i>because you're unsure of your identity?</i>

154
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:10,080
[Louise] Yes.

155
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:13,880
I see. And your file says that
just over two years ago,

156
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:16,880
you were found unconscious at the harbour?

157
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:21,000
Yes. Well, um, I was on a ship,
when it came into the harbour.

158
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:23,760
And you had, uh, serious injuries?

159
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:29,280
Yeah. Yeah, to my neck,
my head, an arm, and my ribs.

160
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:33,680
And you've no idea how you managed
to board the ship, is what it says here?

161
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,760
No.

162
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:38,440
[Louise] <i>I was in hospital</i>
<i>for a long time.</i>

163
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:39,920
<i>Um…</i>

164
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:44,360
And the doctors
then diagnosed me with amnesia.

165
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,360
Then how did the doctors know
who you were?

166
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,960
I still had my bag

167
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:50,040
with a few belongings and my ID.

168
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:52,880
<i>So they told me who I was.</i>

169
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:55,400
-[policewoman] Louise Andersen?
-Yeah.

170
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:59,840
And so the Danish police just accepted
the fact that you were Louise Andersen?

171
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:03,720
Yes, they did, because
I said that they were right.

172
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:10,680
I told them I was Louise
and my memories were coming back to me.

173
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,920
And were they?

174
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:16,720
No, um, I had no idea who I was.

175
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:18,280
Why didn't you say that?

176
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:22,480
Because… It's hard to explain,
but I was afraid.

177
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,720
It's frightening not to know who you are…

178
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:30,160
I guess I hoped that I was her.

179
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,640
And you left it at that?

180
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:36,320
No. I searched for myself online.
There was nothing though.

181
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:39,560
-Nothing?
-There are many Louise Andersens.

182
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:42,600
And the police?
No one contacted family or anything?

183
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,040
Well, I didn't have one.

184
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,520
No next of kin?

185
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:51,120
No. It turned out
I'd… I'd lived a… a hard life.

186
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:55,280
The only records the police had of me were
a couple of arrests in Copenhagen for…

187
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:57,240
for prostitution.

188
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:05,120
I… I have a feeling
I must've been on the run back then.

189
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:09,520
So I came here
to find out who I am and what happened.

190
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,200
Right.

191
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,440
We'll do a DNA test.

192
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,200
[ominous music playing]

193
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:22,840
[policewoman] <i>Your real name</i>
<i>is Helene Söderberg.</i>

194
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:26,880
You disappeared
from your family in Denmark

195
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:28,960
just over two years ago.

196
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:33,040
The Danish police
have been looking for you ever since.

197
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,720
A lot of people have been looking for you.

198
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:39,760
And you're married.

199
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:45,040
You have a son.

200
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:50,520
A son?

201
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:10,480
-[woman] Hi. Joachim Bjørndal? Iben Rask.
-[Joachim] Hi. Yes.

202
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,760
Can you explain it again?

203
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:18,600
[Iben] Because she had an ID
when she was found,

204
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:22,280
unfortunately they didn't investigate
the matter any further.

205
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:25,320
And she confirmed to them
that she was Louise Andersen.

206
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:26,880
[Joachim sighs]

207
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,240
And where… Where is Louise?

208
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:34,640
Oh, wait.
I guess she isn't Louise, is she?

209
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:38,640
No. Helene's now in the care
of the crisis team.

210
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:41,880
You can see her if you like,
but just to reiterate, Joachim…

211
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:44,200
It's definitely her.

212
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,280
The DNA test proved it.

213
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:50,280
We contacted the Danish police
and it's been verified.

214
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:53,520
And we've also notified
her family in Denmark.

215
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,720
Her family?

216
00:14:58,240 --> 00:15:00,240
[mysterious music playing]

217
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:09,280
Apologies. A shorter last name
would've made life easier.

218
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:10,920
[all chuckle]

219
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,040
[woman] Mr. Söderberg? Sorry to interrupt.

220
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,680
-Yes?
-Um, it's urgent I'm afraid.

221
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,080
[Söderberg] Ah. Excuse me.

222
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:24,920
[woman] He'll be right back.

223
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:25,960
Yes?

224
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,600
[mysterious music intensifies]

225
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:34,720
Yes?

226
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:38,760
[sighs]

227
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,880
Did you speak to the police?

228
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:49,640
Yeah. They've explained it all to me, so…

229
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:54,040
It'll be okay.

230
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:57,440
I think Helene's a beautiful name.

231
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:58,640
[both chuckle softly]

232
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:02,160
Well, we'll work through it.

233
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,280
I must go and meet them.

234
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:10,200
[Joachim] Yeah.

235
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:16,040
I have a child.

236
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,480
I'm someone's mother.

237
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:23,600
I have to go to Denmark
and figure out what happened.

238
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:26,280
You're right. Mm.

239
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,080
I understand.

240
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,720
But you know this doesn't change anything.

241
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,440
You and I are getting married.

242
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,800
[dramatic music playing]

243
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:10,800
{\an8}WELCOME TO COPENHAGEN

244
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:16,440
[man] Now then. Are you excited?

245
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:17,520
I am, yeah.

246
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:18,520
[man] Mm?

247
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,560
You look wonderful.

248
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:28,400
-[man] Let me see you.
-Okay.

249
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:32,680
You take it easy. Don't blame her.

250
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:35,360
You know she's been through
a terrible ordeal.

251
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:37,240
I'm sure it must be hard for her.

252
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:50,360
[driver] We're here, Mrs Söderberg.

253
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:53,560
[boy] Is that her?

254
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:57,000
Yes. I presume.

255
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:01,400
[nervous breathing]

256
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:26,560
Hi.

257
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:28,000
-Hi.
-[woman] Welcome.

258
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:35,760
[man] Uh, don't you want to say hi
to your mother, Alexander?

259
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,360
You wanna say hi?

260
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,800
-[man] Don't you want to say hello?
-[woman] Hmm?

261
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:44,080
-[man] Alexander?
-[woman] I'll go after him.

262
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:46,440
Right. Um, this is my mother.

263
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,320
Yeah.

264
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,480
Caroline.

265
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:57,480
It is so good to have you home again.

266
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:06,040
-[man] Uh, will you go check on him?
-[woman] Of course.

267
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:10,000
I'm sure he'll come around.

268
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:13,520
And then there's me, uh… I'm Edmund.

269
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,320
[both chuckle]

270
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:17,240
-Um…
-I guessed you… you were.

271
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:20,480
-It's… It's all a… a bit awkward.
-Yes.

272
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:22,440
[both chuckle nervously]

273
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,000
[Edmund] Mm.

274
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:25,880
You'll come inside?

275
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,880
Yes. [chuckles] Okay.

276
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:30,280
I can take your things.

277
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:31,440
Thanks.

278
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:32,560
Go on in.

279
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:36,800
["Piano Sonata in A Minor, K. 310: II"
by Mozart playing]

280
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:40,280
This is your childhood home.
You grew up here with your father.

281
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:42,880
And that's you and him.

282
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:55,480
[Edmund] This is the piano room.
You used to play here as a child.

283
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:03,520
[sighs] And in here
was your father's study.

284
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:18,280
[Edmund] You don't recognise anything?

285
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:19,880
[Helene] No, not really.

286
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:23,160
Well, um, they said to expect that.

287
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:26,240
I had hoped that
when you saw Alexander and me,

288
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:30,000
you know, things might begin to…
[inhales] …come back.

289
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:33,480
Well, the psychologists hope so.

290
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:35,200
I hope so too.

291
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:41,760
[Helene] Thank you.

292
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:47,840
What happened when I disappeared?

293
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:55,600
Just before you vanished,
your father passed.

294
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:59,720
The man hadn't been well at all.
He went downhill very rapidly and you…

295
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:03,800
you took care of him.
But it was very intense.

296
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:08,600
His passing brought out
a sort of dark bleakness in you.

297
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,520
You had been on medications…

298
00:21:12,360 --> 00:21:15,120
And I think it's possible
you stopped taking them.

299
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:19,160
So you were just spiralling.

300
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:22,840
And then you disappeared.
I spent months looking for you.

301
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:27,840
But in all my searching,
I never had the thought to look abroad,

302
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:29,320
which I will always regret.

303
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:33,680
Helene, this isn't easy
for me to say, but…

304
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:39,200
In the end I told myself
that you had ended it all.

305
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:43,960
It was an option you'd mentioned before.

306
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:46,560
[ominous music playing]

307
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:50,160
Oh… [exhales] I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to bring all this up.

308
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:52,520
It wasn't my intention
to drag up all that…

309
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:55,000
-Uh…
-No, I was the one asking, don't worry.

310
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:56,760
Sorry.

311
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:01,600
Do you… Do you think I could, um…
maybe talk to him?

312
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:06,360
Oh yes, sure. Uh, right.
Up the stairs, first door on your right.

313
00:22:06,880 --> 00:22:08,440
-Thanks.
-Yeah.

314
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:11,520
[door knocking]

315
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,960
[Helene] Alexander?

316
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:17,040
[dreamy atmospheric music playing]

317
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:43,600
You don't remember me?

318
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,600
I will, eventually.

319
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:53,600
Did you miss me?

320
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:59,400
Yeah. I did, in my heart.

321
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:04,080
I'm here now.

322
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:09,880
I won't go away again. Okay?

323
00:23:11,320 --> 00:23:12,320
Mm.

324
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:19,720
[Alexander trembling]

325
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:23,880
-[softly] Oh, Alexander…
-[Alexander sobs softly]

326
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:26,800
You never call me Alexander.

327
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,480
[Helene] Then what do I call you?

328
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:36,120
You really don't know it?

329
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,880
[exhales] I'm trying.

330
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,800
[Helene] <i>Duckling.</i>

331
00:23:48,320 --> 00:23:49,400
Duckling.

332
00:23:52,360 --> 00:23:53,480
Of course.

333
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:04,560
[tense music playing]

334
00:24:07,960 --> 00:24:09,920
[dial tone ringing]

335
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,680
[Iben] <i>Hi, this is Iben Rask.</i>

336
00:24:11,760 --> 00:24:15,480
Hi, hi. It's Joachim.
I recently spoke to you at the hospital.

337
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:17,160
Oh, hi, Joachim.

338
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:18,960
-[Joachim] <i>Hello.</i>
-How is everything?

339
00:24:19,040 --> 00:24:22,920
[Joachim] I just find it a bit strange.
Something's not right.

340
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,840
[Iben] Is that
the crime writer in you talking?

341
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:30,680
No, I mean… Have you tried looking up
her name online? Helene Söderberg?

342
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:32,440
Yes, I did try that.

343
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:34,080
[Joachim] <i>And what did you find?</i>

344
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:38,520
-Yeah, I didn't find too much.
-[Joachim] <i>Exactly. Nothing.</i>

345
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:41,240
[Joachim] I've been searching
for four hours and not a thing.

346
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:44,320
No social media, nothing. It's odd.

347
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:46,680
[Iben] <i>Yeah, I have to say,</i>
<i>I don't disagree with you there.</i>

348
00:24:46,760 --> 00:24:51,160
And then there's her new identity…
This other woman's stolen identity…

349
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:53,760
The real Louise.
What about her? Where is she?

350
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:56,840
Look, her case has already gone over
to the Danish police.

351
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:00,360
So is there…

352
00:25:01,440 --> 00:25:03,680
A contact, or someone
I could speak to over there?

353
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:04,600
[Iben] <i>Yes.</i>

354
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:10,640
Your grandma's on her way.

355
00:25:11,360 --> 00:25:12,480
Good night.

356
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:13,640
[Alexander] Good night.

357
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:26,720
[ominous music playing]

358
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:39,000
[distorted twinkling]

359
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:41,400
[man groans and coughs]

360
00:25:41,480 --> 00:25:42,480
[Edmund] Helene?

361
00:25:51,240 --> 00:25:53,240
[birds tweeting]

362
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:02,480
Is he sleeping?

363
00:26:04,080 --> 00:26:05,080
No.

364
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:08,040
But he let me read to him.

365
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:11,520
Your mother's with him now
until he falls asleep.

366
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:12,800
Right.

367
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:15,160
He's been a little more, um…

368
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:18,080
Mm… Anxious after you vanished.

369
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,440
Um, this wine…

370
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:25,160
It's one of your favourites.

371
00:26:25,960 --> 00:26:27,680
Well it used to be a favourite.

372
00:26:27,760 --> 00:26:29,920
[Helene chuckles softly] Ah.

373
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:35,760
[Edmund] A toast.

374
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:36,800
A toast.

375
00:26:38,520 --> 00:26:39,560
[Helene chuckles]

376
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:42,720
[Edmund] Do you like it?

377
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:43,640
Mm.

378
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:50,400
Um, how long have we been married?

379
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:51,520
[laughs]

380
00:26:51,600 --> 00:26:55,360
Sorry, they probably said already
but it's such a blur.

381
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:57,360
-[Edmund] It's eight years now.
-Woah.

382
00:26:58,200 --> 00:26:59,760
And how did we meet each other?

383
00:26:59,840 --> 00:27:04,600
I worked in your father's business,
uh, and that's where we both worked.

384
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:08,520
And well now… we run the company.

385
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:10,560
We're both on the board of directors.

386
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:13,680
In, um, shipping… I've been told?

387
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:15,080
Yeah, shipping.

388
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:18,600
[inhales] We are the fourth-largest
shipping firm in the North.

389
00:27:21,560 --> 00:27:22,520
[chuckles]

390
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:24,080
[inhales]

391
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:27,320
-So, what do I do there?
-[Edmund laughs]

392
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:30,080
Uh… Um…

393
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:35,080
You were our CFO.
You were very good. Very sharp.

394
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:37,280
-So, in finance?
-[Edmund] Yes.

395
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:39,120
-That's what I did?
-[Edmund] Mm-hmm.

396
00:27:41,360 --> 00:27:43,560
-[Helene] I run a café on the island.
-Mm.

397
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:47,120
That's why business and accounting came
really easily to me, I suppose.

398
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:48,440
-Well, there you go.
-Mm.

399
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:58,520
Um, I don't run it alone. The café. I…

400
00:27:58,600 --> 00:27:59,880
[inhales deeply]

401
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:02,920
I run it with my boyfriend.
Well, my fiancé.

402
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:05,920
Yep, I know. Um… yeah.

403
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:07,880
Joachim.

404
00:28:09,360 --> 00:28:10,200
Yeah.

405
00:28:10,720 --> 00:28:12,520
I see that you're um…

406
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:14,800
You're wearing his ring?

407
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:20,880
Yes. Do you mind?

408
00:28:24,360 --> 00:28:26,400
I'm just glad you're back home again.

409
00:28:27,600 --> 00:28:30,640
And I'm glad
that Alexander has his mother back.

410
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:36,200
Um, and then, then rest
we'll just make work somehow, right?

411
00:28:37,240 --> 00:28:39,280
-Yeah.
-[Edmund] But…

412
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:43,000
I'd really like to show you something.
Bring your wine.

413
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:45,480
-Come on.
-Okay. [chuckles softly]

414
00:28:46,400 --> 00:28:50,680
[Edmund] It's a small film we had made
for you for your birthday a few years ago.

415
00:28:52,760 --> 00:28:53,800
It's your story.

416
00:28:55,120 --> 00:28:56,640
<i>-Hi!</i>
-[man] <i>Hi.</i>

417
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:58,920
[both laughing]

418
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:01,600
[young Helene] <i>I'm flying!</i>

419
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:05,240
[Edmund] You grew up here with your father
after your mother died.

420
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:10,000
She got cancer, sadly, when, um…
when you were very young.

421
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:16,440
But your father adored you,
and he gave you everything you wanted.

422
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:17,520
[chuckling]

423
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:19,320
[Edmund] And you two were inseparable.

424
00:29:20,840 --> 00:29:24,280
And you and I, we… we met at work.

425
00:29:25,320 --> 00:29:26,480
Well, I…

426
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:31,480
I was so intimidated by you.
The boss's beautiful daughter.

427
00:29:31,560 --> 00:29:32,480
[chuckles softly]

428
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:34,480
[chuckles]

429
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:38,520
[Edmund] But I won you over.
And we got married.

430
00:29:39,560 --> 00:29:40,720
We were madly in love.

431
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:43,960
Nothing could keep us apart.

432
00:29:44,040 --> 00:29:45,720
[people cheering on film]

433
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:47,840
[chuckles]

434
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:51,640
[Helene] <i>Feel it, he's kicking now!</i>

435
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:55,320
[Edmund] And then our family was complete
when Alexander came along.

436
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:58,640
We were so happy.

437
00:29:59,240 --> 00:30:00,400
[Edmund chuckles softly]

438
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:04,160
[Helene on film]
<i>His little hands, his nose…</i>

439
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:22,840
[door knocking]

440
00:30:27,080 --> 00:30:29,640
Helene, you'll sleep
in the master bedroom, all right?

441
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:32,320
And I'll make up a guest room for Edmund.

442
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:34,920
I think it's the best option.

443
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:38,280
Wait, Caroline?

444
00:30:38,840 --> 00:30:39,840
Yes?

445
00:30:41,600 --> 00:30:43,560
Thank you for taking care of Alexander.

446
00:30:44,200 --> 00:30:45,680
Oh, but of course.

447
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:48,960
It's truly been a joy.
He's honestly such a delight.

448
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:49,960
[chuckles softly]

449
00:30:51,520 --> 00:30:52,800
And, um…

450
00:30:57,520 --> 00:30:58,720
Was I a good mother?

451
00:31:06,480 --> 00:31:08,160
[Caroline] You were just as you should be.

452
00:31:09,120 --> 00:31:11,920
You listened to him. You adored him.

453
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:19,200
It’s just hard to believe
that I forgot about him.

454
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:23,760
Or that I'd forget
giving birth to my child.

455
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:25,960
You really don't remember anything?

456
00:31:28,640 --> 00:31:31,200
-A few things here and there.
-[Caroline] Well, there you go.

457
00:31:32,040 --> 00:31:35,800
Your head's playing tricks on you
but your heart remembered him.

458
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:40,080
[Caroline] Don't blame yourself.

459
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:42,720
You're here now.

460
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:45,840
[Caroline] Sleep well.

461
00:31:46,920 --> 00:31:48,000
You too.

462
00:32:04,200 --> 00:32:05,200
[sighs]

463
00:32:06,640 --> 00:32:08,640
[dial tone ringing]

464
00:32:10,200 --> 00:32:11,280
[Joachim] <i>Hi.</i>

465
00:32:11,360 --> 00:32:12,400
Hi.

466
00:32:14,080 --> 00:32:15,560
Go on. What's going on?

467
00:32:16,680 --> 00:32:19,280
It's… intense.

468
00:32:20,080 --> 00:32:21,640
[Joachim] I can imagine.

469
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:27,600
But what's it like there?
Are they… nice? Looking after you?

470
00:32:28,480 --> 00:32:30,920
[Helene] <i>It's… really big here.</i>

471
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:32,600
[chuckles softly] And grand.

472
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:36,880
They seem good. And there's Alexander.

473
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:40,200
Yeah.

474
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:47,400
But have you found out
any more answers, or information?

475
00:32:48,440 --> 00:32:50,600
<i>That's why you went to Denmark, isn't it?</i>

476
00:32:50,680 --> 00:32:55,560
Yeah. No, right now,
I'm just trying to navigate it all.

477
00:32:55,640 --> 00:32:58,840
[Joachim] <i>Right, but what happened</i>
<i>when you disappeared?</i>

478
00:32:58,920 --> 00:33:01,680
<i>You have to find out how you ended up</i>
<i>on that ship to Norway.</i>

479
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:03,000
Joachim, I…

480
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:06,000
[sighs]

481
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:09,680
It will have to wait.

482
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:16,680
<i>I can't handle anymore right now.</i>
<i>I'm going to need some more time, okay?</i>

483
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:19,080
Yeah, all right.

484
00:33:22,040 --> 00:33:23,120
I love you.

485
00:33:25,120 --> 00:33:26,120
I love you.

486
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:28,160
[Helene] <i>I'll be in touch, okay? Bye.</i>

487
00:33:35,600 --> 00:33:37,760
[electronic suspenseful music playing]

488
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:58,160
-[Alexander] Bye, Grandma.
-[Caroline] Bye, darling. Bye.

489
00:33:58,800 --> 00:33:59,960
See you.

490
00:34:09,080 --> 00:34:10,280
[Alexander] Hi, David.

491
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:11,520
[David] Hi, Alexander.

492
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:14,120
Look, this is my mum.

493
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:16,720
-What's your name?
-I'm Helene.

494
00:34:16,800 --> 00:34:18,000
She's been home for two days.

495
00:34:18,080 --> 00:34:19,520
-Hi! Hello.
-Ooh.

496
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:21,920
Hello there! Your friends?

497
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:24,920
-[boy] Have you been to the school before?
-[Helene] No, I haven't.

498
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:26,520
-[boy] I've been to Norway too.
-Okay.

499
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:27,800
It's so beautiful.

500
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:29,920
-[bell ringing]
-Bye, Mum.

501
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:33,040
All right, duckling. Have a good day.
Okay, sweetheart?

502
00:34:33,120 --> 00:34:35,280
-[Helene] See you.
-[Alexander] Have a nice day, Mum!

503
00:34:45,160 --> 00:34:47,000
Are you sure you're ready, Helene?

504
00:34:48,720 --> 00:34:52,320
[Helene sighs] Yeah. I'm hoping
it will help me remember.

505
00:34:52,720 --> 00:34:53,560
[Edmund] Okay.

506
00:34:58,360 --> 00:35:00,080
[man 1] Hi, Helene. I'm glad you're back.

507
00:35:00,160 --> 00:35:01,360
Hmm. Thanks.

508
00:35:02,520 --> 00:35:04,000
-[man 2] Good morning.
-Good morning.

509
00:35:04,080 --> 00:35:07,160
Hi, Helene. So good to see you again.

510
00:35:07,240 --> 00:35:08,240
-Good morning.
-Thanks.

511
00:35:08,320 --> 00:35:09,520
Beautiful flowers.

512
00:35:11,240 --> 00:35:12,440
[Peter chatting indistinctly]

513
00:35:14,960 --> 00:35:16,040
[Edmund] Are you okay?

514
00:35:16,120 --> 00:35:20,880
Uh… That man… The one over there
looks a lot like the man who…

515
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:22,320
saw me in Norway.

516
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:25,760
Oh, well it is him.
He works in our compliance department.

517
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:29,640
He was on holiday in Norway
when he saw you. Luckily for us.

518
00:35:30,800 --> 00:35:32,480
Welcome back, Helene.

519
00:35:32,560 --> 00:35:33,560
Thank you.

520
00:35:36,680 --> 00:35:38,680
[intense music playing]

521
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:47,600
[officer] This is the last known photo
of Louise Andersen.

522
00:35:48,240 --> 00:35:52,240
We sent that photo to the Norwegian police
and they identified her, so…

523
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:53,640
Well, that was that.

524
00:35:53,720 --> 00:35:57,520
Okay, but who is she, right?
I mean, who is Louise Andersen?

525
00:35:57,600 --> 00:36:01,000
We have very little on Louise Andersen
other than she was a prostitute.

526
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:02,720
We've listed her as missing,

527
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:05,600
but people in that world
tend to disappear.

528
00:36:05,680 --> 00:36:08,440
It's just… do you think they look alike?

529
00:36:08,960 --> 00:36:10,720
Do you think Helene and Louise look alike?

530
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:12,560
-I'd say a little.
-[Joachim] Oh.

531
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:15,520
Height, hair colour, eye colour.

532
00:36:15,600 --> 00:36:18,760
But most importantly, the officers
involved had no reason to suspect

533
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:21,720
that the woman on the ID wasn't her
when they found her.

534
00:36:21,800 --> 00:36:23,960
Okay. But so, Helene Söderberg, then…

535
00:36:24,040 --> 00:36:26,160
Why didn't you do a bigger search
when she went missing?

536
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:27,960
Well, there weren't many leads.

537
00:36:28,040 --> 00:36:31,920
And our information suggested that
she had committed suicide.

538
00:36:33,720 --> 00:36:35,080
What information?

539
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:36,760
A history of mental illness.

540
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:39,080
Helene Söderberg
was suffering from psychosis

541
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:41,480
when she disappeared. Severe psychosis.

542
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,000
Hello, Mrs Söderberg.

543
00:36:53,200 --> 00:36:55,440
So, Edmund showed you to your old office?

544
00:36:55,520 --> 00:36:56,440
[Helene] Yes.

545
00:36:58,400 --> 00:36:59,400
[both chuckle softly]

546
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:00,520
Ingrid.

547
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:04,400
You don't recognise me?

548
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:05,560
No, sorry.

549
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:08,760
Well… Well,
I suppose we'll just start over.

550
00:37:08,840 --> 00:37:11,920
Ingrid Jensen.
I was your secretary before.

551
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:13,920
And you also worked for my father?

552
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:18,800
Yes. Until he fell sick and then you…
then you took over.

553
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:20,360
Uh, so…

554
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:24,080
I'm so sorry, they said that if we were…

555
00:37:24,160 --> 00:37:28,640
if we were talking of the past,
then we must be careful with it.

556
00:37:28,720 --> 00:37:31,480
Oh, please don't worry, it's no problem.

557
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:34,000
I'm actually trying to remember
as much as possible.

558
00:37:34,080 --> 00:37:35,080
Mm.

559
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:38,600
Ah, well in that case…

560
00:37:41,240 --> 00:37:43,240
Why don't you look in here.

561
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:47,480
It's an anniversary book celebrating
the first ten years of the company.

562
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:48,600
[Helene] Okay.

563
00:37:51,040 --> 00:37:52,280
SÖDERBERG SHIPPING
1967-1977

564
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:57,320
[distorted rumbling]

565
00:37:57,400 --> 00:37:59,400
[both laughing]

566
00:38:00,160 --> 00:38:02,800
[Ingrid] Well, I've brought you
a little of everything.

567
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:05,560
Annual reports and financial statements.

568
00:38:05,640 --> 00:38:08,000
Don't worry, you won't need
to approve anything here.

569
00:38:08,080 --> 00:38:11,560
It's just to give you an idea.
We'll ease you back in.

570
00:38:17,880 --> 00:38:21,000
-[Ingrid] The first pages are…
-The management figures.

571
00:38:21,080 --> 00:38:22,440
That's correct.

572
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:29,000
I see you remember a few things, huh?

573
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:32,720
[chuckles softly] Yeah.

574
00:38:33,440 --> 00:38:35,440
[intense electronic music playing]

575
00:38:47,600 --> 00:38:48,840
POLICE
WANTED AND MISSING PERSONS

576
00:38:48,920 --> 00:38:50,640
MISSING SINCE 2024.
LAST SEEN AROUND HALMTORVET

577
00:38:53,560 --> 00:38:54,640
MISSING SINCE 2024

578
00:38:54,720 --> 00:38:56,440
{\an8}LOUISE ANDERSEN:
SLENDER BUILD, LONG DARK HAIR

579
00:39:06,240 --> 00:39:07,280
{\an8}TRANSPORT AND LOGISTICS LEADER

580
00:39:09,040 --> 00:39:09,880
WHO ARE WE?

581
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:10,880
HISTORY

582
00:39:10,960 --> 00:39:13,280
{\an8}AKSEL SÖDERBERG FOUNDED SÖDERBERG SHIPPING
IN 1967.

583
00:39:17,640 --> 00:39:18,600
IMAGES

584
00:39:28,720 --> 00:39:30,720
NO RESULTS FOR YOUR SEARCH

585
00:39:51,520 --> 00:39:56,760
Hi. Um, do you have any articles
featuring… these keywords?

586
00:39:57,240 --> 00:39:58,400
[librarian] Let me look.

587
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:08,480
-[Joachim] Nothing?
-No, no results, sorry.

588
00:40:09,520 --> 00:40:10,760
Do you hold originals here?

589
00:40:13,360 --> 00:40:14,760
I'll see what I can find.

590
00:40:14,840 --> 00:40:16,840
-Thanks, I'll wait.
-You're welcome.

591
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:19,680
-[Alexander] Come get me!
-[both chuckling]

592
00:40:19,760 --> 00:40:21,200
-[Helene] Go!
-[both chuckling]

593
00:40:21,280 --> 00:40:22,640
[Helene] Come here, you!

594
00:40:24,360 --> 00:40:25,240
[Helene] Right.

595
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:27,480
[Alexander shouting indistinctly]

596
00:40:27,560 --> 00:40:29,520
-[laughing]
-[Helene] Gotcha!

597
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:31,520
[Alexander chuckling]

598
00:40:32,560 --> 00:40:33,680
-[sighs]
-[Caroline chuckles]

599
00:40:33,760 --> 00:40:36,720
-No, no, no. Stop!
-[Alexander laughs] You're it!

600
00:40:37,680 --> 00:40:40,040
[Caroline] Oh, Alexander.

601
00:40:40,640 --> 00:40:42,040
-[Alexander] Ready?
-[Helene] We're ready.

602
00:40:42,120 --> 00:40:43,400
-Ready?
-[both] Yes.

603
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:46,640
-[Helene] You got it? Oh, it's mine.
-[Alexander grunts]

604
00:40:47,240 --> 00:40:49,600
-[Alexander laughs]
-[Helene laughs] We got him!

605
00:40:49,680 --> 00:40:51,880
-[Helene] You got him!
-Come on, Dad.

606
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:53,760
-[Helene] We got him.
-No!

607
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:55,720
-[Alexander] Yeah, we did!
-Watch out! He's up!

608
00:40:58,080 --> 00:40:59,440
-[grunts]
-[phone ringing]

609
00:40:59,520 --> 00:41:02,400
-[Alexander] Yeah!
-[Helene cheers] Well done.

610
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:04,600
-[Edmund] Hold on, hold on, hold on.
-High five!

611
00:41:04,680 --> 00:41:06,680
-[Alexander] Yeah. [chuckles]
-Nice work. [chuckles]

612
00:41:06,760 --> 00:41:08,440
Uh, I need to get this.

613
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:09,800
[Alexander] No, Dad…

614
00:41:09,880 --> 00:41:11,760
-[Edmund] Hello?
-[Alexander groans]

615
00:41:12,840 --> 00:41:14,280
[Helene] Your shoelace is untied.

616
00:41:16,080 --> 00:41:19,160
-You're good at tennis.
-[Alexander] Thanks.

617
00:41:20,640 --> 00:41:22,560
[Alexander] Are you still mad at Dad?

618
00:41:22,640 --> 00:41:23,600
Mad how?

619
00:41:24,880 --> 00:41:28,080
You screamed at him
right before you disappeared.

620
00:41:30,280 --> 00:41:31,320
You were there?

621
00:41:31,960 --> 00:41:34,240
Yes. It was at night.

622
00:41:38,040 --> 00:41:42,640
Look, parents do argue.
I'm sure there was no need to worry.

623
00:41:44,160 --> 00:41:45,920
[sighs] You were arguing over me.

624
00:41:47,160 --> 00:41:49,080
None of this is your fault.

625
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:52,680
You know that?

626
00:41:56,400 --> 00:41:57,400
Okay.

627
00:41:57,480 --> 00:41:59,400
[gentle music playing]

628
00:42:01,800 --> 00:42:03,680
[Helene] Mm. Can I taste it?

629
00:42:03,760 --> 00:42:05,240
[Edmund] Mm-hmm. Try it.

630
00:42:07,120 --> 00:42:08,880
-[Edmund] Delicious, isn't it?
-Mm.

631
00:42:11,920 --> 00:42:15,720
[Edmund] I made you this
on our very first date.

632
00:42:16,360 --> 00:42:17,240
[Helene] Mm.

633
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:28,760
[door knocking]

634
00:42:47,200 --> 00:42:49,200
[breathes deeply]

635
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,680
[Edmund sighs]

636
00:43:10,560 --> 00:43:11,840
I've missed you, Helene.

637
00:43:14,520 --> 00:43:16,520
[sombre string music playing]

638
00:43:31,320 --> 00:43:33,320
[music intensifies]

639
00:43:48,560 --> 00:43:51,680
[Helene] I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

640
00:43:51,760 --> 00:43:53,040
[music steadies]

641
00:43:54,880 --> 00:43:55,880
I'm sorry.

642
00:44:03,400 --> 00:44:06,880
-I… I didn't mean…
-No, no, it's all right.

643
00:44:09,040 --> 00:44:11,120
You aren't ready. It's fine.

644
00:44:18,720 --> 00:44:20,000
[sighs]

645
00:44:21,040 --> 00:44:21,960
[sighs]

646
00:44:23,960 --> 00:44:25,960
[thunder rumbling]

647
00:44:30,720 --> 00:44:32,200
[distorted rumbling]

648
00:44:32,280 --> 00:44:35,480
[Aksel struggling]

649
00:44:35,560 --> 00:44:36,680
[mumbling] Come here.

650
00:44:36,760 --> 00:44:38,120
[inhales deeply]

651
00:44:50,280 --> 00:44:53,400
[eerie piano music playing]

652
00:45:02,320 --> 00:45:03,400
[distant knocking]

653
00:45:12,320 --> 00:45:13,400
[distant commotion]

654
00:45:46,800 --> 00:45:48,120
[rumbling becomes closer]

655
00:45:54,400 --> 00:45:57,960
[ominous music intensifies]

656
00:46:12,400 --> 00:46:13,640
[creaking]

657
00:46:21,120 --> 00:46:23,120
[window creaks]

658
00:46:34,840 --> 00:46:39,880
[distorted rumbling]

659
00:46:39,960 --> 00:46:41,920
[laboured breathing]

660
00:46:42,000 --> 00:46:44,480
Listen. It's important.

661
00:46:54,120 --> 00:46:56,560
-Helene? All okay?
-[gasps]

662
00:46:56,640 --> 00:46:59,120
[sighs] Yeah.

663
00:47:00,240 --> 00:47:02,200
You should be asleep.

664
00:47:02,840 --> 00:47:05,320
My father was up here, wasn't he?

665
00:47:06,160 --> 00:47:08,520
He moved to the tower room
when he got sick.

666
00:47:09,240 --> 00:47:11,160
He wanted a view of the forest.

667
00:47:11,240 --> 00:47:13,280
You said it soothed him.

668
00:47:14,000 --> 00:47:15,160
Do you know…

669
00:47:16,560 --> 00:47:20,720
What he said to me, at the end?
I mean, right before he died?

670
00:47:20,800 --> 00:47:25,920
No, I don't know, my dear.
I didn't know your father all that well.

671
00:47:28,320 --> 00:47:30,440
SUSPICIOUS DEATH
DIED IN HIS OWN HOME

672
00:47:32,080 --> 00:47:34,920
-[officer] Where did you get these?
-National Library.

673
00:47:35,000 --> 00:47:35,920
[officer] Mm-hmm.

674
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:39,520
All the digital archives were erased.
Which is a bit weird, don't you think?

675
00:47:40,120 --> 00:47:42,000
So I had to make copies
from the actual newspapers.

676
00:47:42,080 --> 00:47:43,720
[inhales deeply] Right.

677
00:47:43,800 --> 00:47:45,680
And how can I help, then?

678
00:47:47,720 --> 00:47:50,160
Well, I want to know
if you ever looked into that?

679
00:47:51,360 --> 00:47:52,400
What exactly?

680
00:47:52,480 --> 00:47:55,760
About… [laughs awkwardly]
…Helen's father. The way he died.

681
00:47:55,840 --> 00:47:57,920
Well, it says he was found dead at home.

682
00:47:58,000 --> 00:48:01,160
We looked into it,
but concluded that it was an accident.

683
00:48:02,040 --> 00:48:03,400
There's no more to that case.

684
00:48:03,480 --> 00:48:04,960
Yeah, but I have more evidence.

685
00:48:06,600 --> 00:48:08,520
Louise… Um, Helene… [sighs]

686
00:48:08,600 --> 00:48:12,320
Helene was found aboard a ship.
This ship here.

687
00:48:12,920 --> 00:48:15,600
Did any of you look into
how she came to be aboard that ship?

688
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:20,360
[scoffs] You mean how she got on board
a Norwegian ship several years ago?

689
00:48:21,600 --> 00:48:23,800
[sighs] There's no way I could know that.

690
00:48:23,880 --> 00:48:26,280
No, I understand that, but…

691
00:48:27,360 --> 00:48:29,920
I can feel it. There's more going on.

692
00:48:30,600 --> 00:48:32,800
I know it. So will you help me?

693
00:48:35,360 --> 00:48:38,720
I expect she boarded
from one of the harbours along its route.

694
00:48:39,240 --> 00:48:43,160
If I were you, I'd locate the ship's log
and then you can check the route it took.

695
00:48:43,960 --> 00:48:45,520
There's nothing else we can do.

696
00:48:45,600 --> 00:48:47,480
[ominous electronic music rises, fades]

697
00:48:48,080 --> 00:48:50,320
[Alexander] Ten, thirty…

698
00:48:51,360 --> 00:48:53,280
What about that one? What is it?

699
00:48:53,360 --> 00:48:55,480
Alexander, we need to go.
Can you get ready?

700
00:48:55,560 --> 00:48:56,600
[Alexander] Okay.

701
00:48:58,680 --> 00:49:00,480
Yeah. Off you go.

702
00:49:05,160 --> 00:49:06,160
Good morning.

703
00:49:09,800 --> 00:49:11,000
I'll check on him.

704
00:49:16,800 --> 00:49:18,680
Your mother seems so wonderful, Edmund.

705
00:49:20,760 --> 00:49:23,640
I'm glad she was with Alexander
while I was away.

706
00:49:23,720 --> 00:49:24,840
[Edmund] Yes.

707
00:49:26,200 --> 00:49:27,800
[Helene] By the way, I was thinking…

708
00:49:28,880 --> 00:49:32,440
We haven't really spoken about
my father, you know?

709
00:49:32,520 --> 00:49:33,960
How he died.

710
00:49:35,760 --> 00:49:40,600
You and Alexander were alone
in the house that day.

711
00:49:41,760 --> 00:49:44,440
And no one really knows what happened.

712
00:49:45,040 --> 00:49:48,400
But we think he might have been trying
to leave his room

713
00:49:48,480 --> 00:49:51,440
and he fell… down the stairs.

714
00:49:52,120 --> 00:49:52,960
[gasps]

715
00:49:54,360 --> 00:49:56,440
So it was me who found him or…?

716
00:49:56,520 --> 00:50:00,040
[Edmund] Yes.
I've been withholding the details.

717
00:50:00,120 --> 00:50:03,000
It was violently traumatising for you.

718
00:50:05,080 --> 00:50:09,240
My darling, I don't want you to go back
to that dark place again.

719
00:50:09,320 --> 00:50:11,320
[ominous music playing]

720
00:50:20,800 --> 00:50:23,800
{\an8}OUR EMPLOYEES PHOTOGRAPHED
IN FRONT OF THE OFFICES ON WILDERS STREET

721
00:50:32,320 --> 00:50:35,560
Ingrid, how come there's pages missing?

722
00:50:35,640 --> 00:50:38,200
Oh. No idea.

723
00:50:40,120 --> 00:50:43,960
I've got another copy at home
from when I first began working here.

724
00:50:44,040 --> 00:50:45,840
I can see if they're in there,
if you'd like?

725
00:50:47,000 --> 00:50:49,400
That would be great. Thank you.

726
00:50:52,320 --> 00:50:54,200
-Um, Ingrid?
-Yeah?

727
00:50:56,440 --> 00:50:59,400
What was I doing before I disappeared?

728
00:51:00,080 --> 00:51:01,640
Uh… Uh…

729
00:51:03,080 --> 00:51:08,240
Uh… Oh, I think it's best if you…
talk to your husband about it, yes?

730
00:51:16,680 --> 00:51:19,240
It's only that I'd really like to know…

731
00:51:20,160 --> 00:51:22,360
your view of what… what happened.

732
00:51:26,240 --> 00:51:27,560
Uh, well…

733
00:51:28,680 --> 00:51:31,440
[inhales] I can only really tell you
what you said to me.

734
00:51:31,520 --> 00:51:32,760
Mm-hmm.

735
00:51:34,760 --> 00:51:38,800
Well, he tried to speak to you about
something important right before he died.

736
00:51:39,360 --> 00:51:44,280
On his deathbed, he drifted
in and out of consciousness, so…

737
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:46,920
he would forget
what he'd already said to you,

738
00:51:47,000 --> 00:51:49,400
and so he ran out of time
to tell you it all.

739
00:51:49,480 --> 00:51:51,520
[mysterious music playing]

740
00:51:51,600 --> 00:51:52,600
Hmm.

741
00:51:54,200 --> 00:51:59,920
And then right before you vanished…
it seemed like you were obsessed.

742
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:02,440
How? What… What was I doing?

743
00:52:03,040 --> 00:52:06,560
You were convinced that he had…
a warning, a confession.

744
00:52:07,800 --> 00:52:10,360
That there was something
you needed to know before he died

745
00:52:10,440 --> 00:52:11,920
and you took over the company.

746
00:52:12,680 --> 00:52:16,760
Then, after he passed,
you combed through everything here.

747
00:52:17,600 --> 00:52:21,560
Contracts, transactions, every client,
all of the routes. I mean it.

748
00:52:22,160 --> 00:52:27,160
All of it. You became more and more…
It pains me to say it, but…

749
00:52:28,880 --> 00:52:31,720
you seemed manic, to tell the truth.

750
00:52:32,720 --> 00:52:34,240
You were working day and night.

751
00:52:35,480 --> 00:52:36,720
And what about Edmund?

752
00:52:38,200 --> 00:52:42,640
[sighs] Edmund, he…
He tried to ease your mind.

753
00:52:43,840 --> 00:52:46,400
Reassure you it was okay.

754
00:52:46,480 --> 00:52:48,560
So that's why I disappeared.

755
00:52:48,640 --> 00:52:49,920
Uh… Sorry, I…

756
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:54,320
I discovered something.
His death wasn't why I broke down.

757
00:52:55,960 --> 00:52:57,680
I can only say what I saw.

758
00:52:57,760 --> 00:52:58,760
Yes.

759
00:53:02,520 --> 00:53:06,440
[distorted rumbling]

760
00:53:06,520 --> 00:53:07,640
[gasps]

761
00:53:17,880 --> 00:53:21,840
Ingrid, I'd like to know precisely what
I was doing before I disappeared.

762
00:53:21,920 --> 00:53:23,760
What I was working on and who I met with.

763
00:53:24,320 --> 00:53:26,120
Yes. I'll find your old diary.

764
00:53:26,200 --> 00:53:27,480
Thanks.

765
00:53:27,560 --> 00:53:30,640
[Ingrid] I do remember one thing though.
Your last meeting was with the bank.

766
00:53:31,320 --> 00:53:34,240
You were saying
that meeting was important to you…

767
00:53:35,080 --> 00:53:36,800
Yes, I remember finding it strange

768
00:53:36,880 --> 00:53:39,120
that you weren't meeting with
Söderberg's branch

769
00:53:39,200 --> 00:53:41,040
who we dealt with normally.

770
00:53:41,120 --> 00:53:41,960
[Helene] Okay.

771
00:53:42,040 --> 00:53:45,040
Okay. Could you find the name of the bank,
and my calendar?

772
00:53:45,120 --> 00:53:46,240
[Ingrid] Of course.

773
00:53:46,960 --> 00:53:48,480
[footsteps retreating]

774
00:53:50,160 --> 00:53:51,760
-[bank teller] Mrs Söderberg?
-Hi.

775
00:53:51,840 --> 00:53:54,080
[bank teller] It's been a while.
Good to see you again.

776
00:53:54,160 --> 00:53:55,120
Likewise.

777
00:53:56,520 --> 00:53:58,600
So, how can we help you today?

778
00:53:59,520 --> 00:54:01,440
-When I last was here, um…
-Mm.

779
00:54:02,320 --> 00:54:04,160
What did I say to you?

780
00:54:04,760 --> 00:54:08,160
Uh, do you mean when you set up
your safe-deposit box?

781
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:11,080
Yeah. That time.

782
00:54:12,120 --> 00:54:14,040
Yeah, what exactly was our agreement?

783
00:54:14,600 --> 00:54:16,640
[bank teller] Well,
there was no agreement as such.

784
00:54:16,720 --> 00:54:19,280
You just set up a safe-deposit box.

785
00:54:20,040 --> 00:54:21,920
And you didn't want your husband to know.

786
00:54:24,480 --> 00:54:25,960
That was it, yeah.

787
00:54:28,840 --> 00:54:30,840
[mysterious music playing]

788
00:54:48,800 --> 00:54:51,120
PRENUPTIAL AGREEMENT

789
00:55:17,280 --> 00:55:19,280
[phone ringing]

790
00:55:20,720 --> 00:55:23,240
-[Helene] Yes, Ingrid?
-[Ingrid] <i>I found your old calendar.</i>

791
00:55:23,320 --> 00:55:24,360
And?

792
00:55:24,440 --> 00:55:26,080
<i>In the days before you disappeared,</i>

793
00:55:26,160 --> 00:55:28,920
<i>you had a meeting</i>
<i>with someone called Elisabeth Fauerskov.</i>

794
00:55:29,000 --> 00:55:30,920
-<i>Does that ring a bell?</i>
-Not at all.

795
00:55:31,000 --> 00:55:35,520
<i>She was the CEO of</i>
<i>one of our sub-contractors, JM Shipping.</i>

796
00:55:35,600 --> 00:55:37,800
<i>And I believe she knew your husband.</i>

797
00:55:37,880 --> 00:55:38,960
Okay?

798
00:55:39,040 --> 00:55:41,960
<i>-Anyway, I'm sending you her details now.</i>
-Okay. Thanks for that.

799
00:55:42,040 --> 00:55:43,320
-Right, bye.
-Thank you.

800
00:55:45,880 --> 00:55:47,440
[notification chimes]

801
00:55:52,440 --> 00:55:54,360
[dial tone ringing]

802
00:55:54,440 --> 00:55:58,280
-[Elisabeth] <i>Elisabeth Fauerskov.</i>
-Hi, Elisabeth. I am Helene Söderberg.

803
00:55:58,360 --> 00:56:00,760
-I'm calling to speak…
<i>-I… I don't want to talk to you.</i>

804
00:56:00,840 --> 00:56:03,160
<i>-Don't contact me.</i>
-[call disconnects]

805
00:56:05,600 --> 00:56:06,480
[scoffs]

806
00:56:10,440 --> 00:56:11,560
[dial tone ringing]

807
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:13,280
[call disconnects]

808
00:56:29,960 --> 00:56:34,880
[mysterious music playing]

809
00:56:35,480 --> 00:56:37,520
[distorted rumbling]

810
00:56:44,160 --> 00:56:46,360
SHIP ROUTE INFO

811
00:56:56,040 --> 00:56:59,040
FYKSESUND BRIDGE

812
00:57:13,240 --> 00:57:15,240
[dial tone ringing]

813
00:57:15,960 --> 00:57:18,640
[Helene] Charlie's not my dad,
he's more like…

814
00:57:18,720 --> 00:57:20,680
[Helene] <i>Hi, I can't come</i>
<i>to the phone right now.</i>

815
00:57:20,760 --> 00:57:22,080
<i>Please leave a message.</i>

816
00:57:22,160 --> 00:57:23,400
[voicemail beeping]

817
00:57:23,480 --> 00:57:25,080
[Joachim] <i>Hi, Helene. It's me.</i>

818
00:57:25,800 --> 00:57:27,720
<i>I know you said you needed time,</i>

819
00:57:28,320 --> 00:57:31,200
<i>but I've found something very important</i>
<i>that you really need to hear.</i>

820
00:57:31,760 --> 00:57:33,280
<i>Call me as soon as you can.</i>

821
00:58:18,760 --> 00:58:20,200
-Thank you.
-[Edmund] Cheers.

822
00:58:20,280 --> 00:58:21,440
Cheers.

823
00:58:26,160 --> 00:58:28,080
You wanted to ask me something?

824
00:58:29,560 --> 00:58:31,760
Yes, um…

825
00:58:35,160 --> 00:58:36,160
Were…

826
00:58:37,800 --> 00:58:39,120
Were we separating?

827
00:58:41,400 --> 00:58:42,440
Sorry?

828
00:58:43,280 --> 00:58:47,640
Before I went missing, um…
Was divorce something we discussed?

829
00:58:47,720 --> 00:58:49,080
Uh, what makes you say that?

830
00:58:49,160 --> 00:58:53,600
I just got this feeling. Like a flashback.

831
00:58:54,200 --> 00:58:55,240
A flashback?

832
00:58:55,960 --> 00:58:56,960
[Helene] Mm-hmm.

833
00:58:57,920 --> 00:59:00,240
Okay? Pretty interesting.

834
00:59:01,240 --> 00:59:03,440
[Edmund breathes deeply]

835
00:59:04,080 --> 00:59:06,200
Mm… Were we divorcing?

836
00:59:06,280 --> 00:59:07,840
No! No.

837
00:59:07,920 --> 00:59:08,920
[Helene] No.

838
00:59:10,400 --> 00:59:11,280
Okay.

839
00:59:11,360 --> 00:59:12,360
No way.

840
00:59:13,920 --> 00:59:17,240
Who is… Elisabeth Fauerskov?

841
00:59:17,320 --> 00:59:21,360
Um… She was the director
at one of our sub-contractors.

842
00:59:21,440 --> 00:59:25,120
Hm. And you knew her personally?

843
00:59:25,200 --> 00:59:28,760
Yes, I knew her from back in school.

844
00:59:30,400 --> 00:59:32,960
And do you know why she won't talk to me?

845
00:59:33,680 --> 00:59:34,880
You've lost me.

846
00:59:34,960 --> 00:59:37,800
She was one of the last people
I spoke to before I disappeared,

847
00:59:37,880 --> 00:59:39,960
so I phoned her today and um…

848
00:59:40,480 --> 00:59:42,400
She wouldn't talk to me at all.
She hung up, so…

849
00:59:42,480 --> 00:59:46,200
Okay, but there's actually a…
a simple reason for that. Um…

850
00:59:47,200 --> 00:59:53,600
We stopped working with them after…
they broke a trade-restraint clause,

851
00:59:53,680 --> 00:59:56,400
so she's not allowed
to speak to you by law.

852
00:59:59,400 --> 01:00:00,440
Oh.

853
01:00:01,680 --> 01:00:02,760
My love…

854
01:00:04,480 --> 01:00:08,480
Now please stop.
Don't embroil yourself with that again.

855
01:00:10,120 --> 01:00:13,680
You'll get tangled in a web of delusions
that lead to nowhere.

856
01:00:13,760 --> 01:00:16,040
-[scoffs] What?
-You're very upset.

857
01:00:16,120 --> 01:00:18,160
[scoffs] No, I'm not upset at all.

858
01:00:22,880 --> 01:00:24,440
Did we argue over her?

859
01:00:25,280 --> 01:00:28,800
Alexander told me we were arguing
before I disappeared, and..

860
01:00:29,560 --> 01:00:32,720
I thought perhaps we were arguing about
her and there was something going on?

861
01:00:33,280 --> 01:00:36,160
It's all in your mind.
I mean, Helene, you sound paranoid.

862
01:00:36,240 --> 01:00:38,480
I'm only asking a few questions here.

863
01:00:38,560 --> 01:00:39,560
Okay.

864
01:00:40,840 --> 01:00:42,600
[sighs]

865
01:00:42,680 --> 01:00:48,280
[clears throat] I've tried saying it
as gently as possible, but I'll try again.

866
01:00:49,560 --> 01:00:51,040
You are ill, Helene.

867
01:00:52,440 --> 01:00:53,440
[exhales]

868
01:00:55,480 --> 01:00:57,480
What are you trying to say?

869
01:00:57,560 --> 01:01:01,560
You have a form of personality disorder,
like schizophrenia.

870
01:01:01,640 --> 01:01:05,120
The doctors think
that maybe it's always been there…

871
01:01:05,200 --> 01:01:08,080
And um, the abrupt death
of your father triggered you.

872
01:01:08,160 --> 01:01:09,520
I am not schizophrenic.

873
01:01:09,600 --> 01:01:10,760
-[Edmund] Look…
-No!

874
01:01:13,560 --> 01:01:16,320
-So how do you explain it?
-Explain what?

875
01:01:17,640 --> 01:01:19,000
Helene, you left your family.

876
01:01:20,320 --> 01:01:25,960
You went to Norway. New name, new house.
You started a whole new life.

877
01:01:26,040 --> 01:01:27,720
Yeah, yeah, Edmund I had amnesia.

878
01:01:27,800 --> 01:01:28,720
[sighs]

879
01:01:30,320 --> 01:01:33,800
Mm-hmm. From hitting your head?

880
01:01:33,880 --> 01:01:35,360
-[Helene] Yes.
-Ah.

881
01:01:35,440 --> 01:01:37,840
Then you woke up on a ship.

882
01:01:37,920 --> 01:01:39,400
[distorted rumbling]

883
01:01:39,480 --> 01:01:41,880
-Can you hear yourself?
-Yeah. [exhales]

884
01:01:41,960 --> 01:01:46,080
[echoing] It's not really a sane person
who does that, is it?

885
01:01:46,160 --> 01:01:48,360
I don't feel good. Um, I need air.

886
01:01:48,440 --> 01:01:50,920
-Here. Um, sit down.
- Can we go outside?

887
01:01:51,000 --> 01:01:52,720
-Take a breath. Breathe.
-No, I want…

888
01:01:52,800 --> 01:01:54,960
-Try to calm down.
-No, I just want some fresh air.

889
01:01:55,040 --> 01:01:57,040
I want some fresh air.
Will you please just--

890
01:01:57,120 --> 01:01:59,040
-[grunts]
-[Helene yelps]

891
01:01:59,720 --> 01:02:01,000
That's enough now!

892
01:02:01,520 --> 01:02:03,520
[panicked breathing]

893
01:02:04,520 --> 01:02:06,040
[Edmund] That's enough.

894
01:02:06,800 --> 01:02:10,880
Helene, I won't accept…
that you decimate our family again.

895
01:02:10,960 --> 01:02:14,640
[ominous music rises]

896
01:02:15,920 --> 01:02:16,960
[Helene sobs]

897
01:02:19,600 --> 01:02:22,560
It's okay. It's okay, it's okay…

898
01:02:24,760 --> 01:02:27,840
[Edmund] Come on, let's go upstairs.
You need to rest.

899
01:02:57,680 --> 01:02:59,680
[music intensifies]

900
01:03:14,440 --> 01:03:16,240
[musik kulminerer]

901
01:03:16,320 --> 01:03:18,480
[breathing deeply]

902
01:03:18,560 --> 01:03:20,560
[doorbell ringing]

903
01:03:33,040 --> 01:03:36,600
-Hi. You okay?
-[Joachim] Hi there. I'm Joachim.

904
01:03:36,680 --> 01:03:39,200
-[Edmund] Joachim?
-Yes, uh, you know of me?

905
01:03:39,280 --> 01:03:40,600
-Yes. I do.
-Right.

906
01:03:40,680 --> 01:03:44,800
I just wanted to, um, speak to Helene.

907
01:03:45,760 --> 01:03:46,800
[exhales]

908
01:03:48,640 --> 01:03:49,680
Um…

909
01:03:50,920 --> 01:03:52,560
Well, she's already gone to bed.

910
01:03:54,320 --> 01:03:56,840
-Okay. She's asleep already?
-[Edmund] Mm-hmm. Yes.

911
01:03:56,920 --> 01:04:01,160
Helene's gone through…
Well, quite a hard time.

912
01:04:01,880 --> 01:04:02,880
Mm.

913
01:04:02,960 --> 01:04:04,680
I'm… I'm sure she has.

914
01:04:05,360 --> 01:04:09,400
So if you want to talk to her,
might be best to come back another time.

915
01:04:09,480 --> 01:04:14,000
-Then I'll come back tomorrow to see her.
-I think she'll need more time than that.

916
01:04:15,120 --> 01:04:17,440
I'll have her get back to you
as soon as possible. Okay?

917
01:04:18,800 --> 01:04:20,280
But Joachim, um…

918
01:04:21,320 --> 01:04:23,600
Since you're already here…
[chuckles softly]

919
01:04:23,680 --> 01:04:26,760
Uh, actually,
I'd love to speak to you about something.

920
01:04:27,240 --> 01:04:28,520
Have you got a minute?

921
01:04:30,280 --> 01:04:33,120
-Of course.
-Come in. Hmm?

922
01:04:41,600 --> 01:04:44,000
[Edmund] This is my mother, Caroline.

923
01:04:45,600 --> 01:04:46,720
[Caroline] Good evening.

924
01:04:47,720 --> 01:04:50,000
-Uh, let's go in here. Yeah?
-Sure.

925
01:04:52,200 --> 01:04:54,200
[breathing echoes]

926
01:04:56,560 --> 01:04:57,600
Joachim…

927
01:04:58,520 --> 01:05:01,720
-Is, um, is that for her? That folder?
-[Joachim] Yeah.

928
01:05:01,800 --> 01:05:04,080
-[Edmund] Mm-hmm.
-I've been trying to…

929
01:05:05,320 --> 01:05:07,440
Well, just kind of work it out.

930
01:05:07,520 --> 01:05:10,800
Yes. Of course.
Um, shall we look at it now, or--

931
01:05:10,880 --> 01:05:13,400
No, I'll talk directly with Helene, so…

932
01:05:16,000 --> 01:05:17,520
[exhales]

933
01:05:18,400 --> 01:05:19,320
[Helene] Joachim…

934
01:05:19,400 --> 01:05:21,240
[Edmund] Anything you'd like to ask me?

935
01:05:21,320 --> 01:05:24,280
Since you've been putting in
all that effort to…

936
01:05:25,440 --> 01:05:27,000
work it out, as you said.

937
01:05:27,080 --> 01:05:31,680
I was wondering why
you didn't go public when she…

938
01:05:31,760 --> 01:05:34,840
when she vanished. It's a bit… weird

939
01:05:35,720 --> 01:05:38,680
We were convinced that
Helene had ended it all.

940
01:05:39,520 --> 01:05:41,920
And I didn't want that
dragged through the press.

941
01:05:42,000 --> 01:05:45,480
Particularly for Alexander's sake.
He's our son.

942
01:05:45,560 --> 01:05:48,520
-And what about her father?
-[Edmund] What about him?

943
01:05:48,600 --> 01:05:52,480
The news of his death,
you also kept that news so quiet…

944
01:05:52,560 --> 01:05:54,440
-I would say.
-[Edmund] Yes, you're not wrong.

945
01:05:55,280 --> 01:05:58,080
It really was an unworthy death
for a man of his calibre.

946
01:05:58,160 --> 01:06:00,480
That's why we didn't go public with it.

947
01:06:00,560 --> 01:06:05,000
[chuckles] It's… so… fascinating.

948
01:06:05,080 --> 01:06:06,400
Fascinating?

949
01:06:06,480 --> 01:06:10,080
Well how do you do it?
There's nothing about any of you online.

950
01:06:10,160 --> 01:06:13,280
If you search, there's nothing.
It's like the whole family doesn't exist.

951
01:06:13,360 --> 01:06:14,320
[banging]

952
01:06:16,160 --> 01:06:17,120
[Helene groaning]

953
01:06:18,280 --> 01:06:23,360
Uh, yes.
Um, there's a reason for that as well.

954
01:06:25,400 --> 01:06:26,520
We had it erased.

955
01:06:26,600 --> 01:06:29,240
We have a department
in the company that handles that.

956
01:06:29,320 --> 01:06:30,320
[scoffs]

957
01:06:31,440 --> 01:06:32,560
But why?

958
01:06:32,640 --> 01:06:35,520
[Edmund] <i>We don't think</i>
<i>the tragedies of the Söderberg family</i>

959
01:06:35,600 --> 01:06:38,040
<i>should be a public spectacle.</i>

960
01:06:40,200 --> 01:06:41,040
[Helene grunts]

961
01:06:42,240 --> 01:06:45,120
[Edmund] Joachim, I understand
that this is hard for you.

962
01:06:45,200 --> 01:06:47,800
You've lost the woman that you love.

963
01:06:47,880 --> 01:06:52,440
What I can say is that
Helene always hurts people, unfortunately.

964
01:06:52,520 --> 01:06:54,360
Even if it's not her intention.

965
01:06:54,440 --> 01:06:57,120
That's why I have a proposal.

966
01:06:57,200 --> 01:06:58,640
[Helene, echoing] Joachim…

967
01:07:00,240 --> 01:07:02,160
I gather you ran a café with her?

968
01:07:02,240 --> 01:07:05,560
Which is now closed?
Because you can't run it alone.

969
01:07:05,640 --> 01:07:11,160
I was also told that you've spent
several years working on a book too?

970
01:07:14,600 --> 01:07:15,840
Hang on, uh…

971
01:07:15,920 --> 01:07:18,760
[scoffs] I don't see how that's relevant,
to be honest with you…

972
01:07:18,840 --> 01:07:22,440
Joachim, I'll be blunt.
I have money that can help you.

973
01:07:22,520 --> 01:07:25,080
-[banging]
-[Helene grunting]

974
01:07:25,160 --> 01:07:28,760
[Edmund] So I've had
an agreement drafted up. Um…

975
01:07:30,360 --> 01:07:35,160
Which, financially speaking,
is quite lucrative for you.

976
01:07:45,200 --> 01:07:46,040
CONFIDENTIALITY AGREEMENT

977
01:07:46,120 --> 01:07:48,280
[Edmund] We'd like to ensure
that Helene's disappearance,

978
01:07:48,360 --> 01:07:53,000
and the tragedy of our family
doesn't end up making it into a book

979
01:07:53,080 --> 01:07:54,760
or any kind of colourful story, you see.

980
01:07:54,840 --> 01:07:56,000
[banging]

981
01:07:56,080 --> 01:07:58,720
[Edmund] You and I have been through
some tragic events.

982
01:07:58,800 --> 01:08:02,520
But this has hurt Alexander most of all.
I've tried to shield him.

983
01:08:03,960 --> 01:08:06,360
And I intend to keep it that way.

984
01:08:09,560 --> 01:08:14,280
You can keep your hard-earned money,
'cause I'm gonna leave now.

985
01:08:15,440 --> 01:08:16,400
[Joachim sighs]

986
01:08:17,960 --> 01:08:21,440
Uh, tell me. Are you under the influence?

987
01:08:23,880 --> 01:08:26,280
Perhaps you would like to sit down
for a little while.

988
01:08:26,360 --> 01:08:27,600
I haven't been drinking.

989
01:08:27,680 --> 01:08:29,680
-[ominous music playing]
-[Helene grunting]

990
01:08:32,400 --> 01:08:33,760
You haven't had a drink?

991
01:08:35,600 --> 01:08:36,600
No.

992
01:08:36,680 --> 01:08:37,640
[Edmund] Okay.

993
01:08:37,720 --> 01:08:39,440
[Helene mumbling]

994
01:08:39,520 --> 01:08:43,040
I'm not judging you. It would be
completely fair and understandable

995
01:08:43,120 --> 01:08:45,240
if you had felt the need
to have a drink today.

996
01:08:45,320 --> 01:08:47,600
-Well, I haven't. I've been fine.
-No?

997
01:08:47,680 --> 01:08:49,120
-Okay.
-[Joachim] Yeah.

998
01:08:50,960 --> 01:08:52,040
Goodbye.

999
01:08:53,160 --> 01:08:54,840
-You know your way out?
-[Joachim] Yeah.

1000
01:08:55,880 --> 01:08:58,920
[ominous music intensifies]

1001
01:09:02,480 --> 01:09:06,120
[music builds]

1002
01:09:06,760 --> 01:09:09,000
[loud clattering]

1003
01:09:15,560 --> 01:09:21,160
[panting]

1004
01:09:21,240 --> 01:09:22,440
[Helene] Joachim…

1005
01:09:22,520 --> 01:09:24,280
[footsteps approaching]

1006
01:09:25,560 --> 01:09:27,240
Helene, what's wrong?

1007
01:09:35,240 --> 01:09:37,040
Helene, come with me, darling.

1008
01:09:38,880 --> 01:09:40,240
Let's get you back to bed.

1009
01:09:42,840 --> 01:09:44,400
[Caroline] What are you saying?

1010
01:09:44,480 --> 01:09:45,440
[Helene] Edmund…

1011
01:09:46,160 --> 01:09:47,160
Edmund?

1012
01:09:48,360 --> 01:09:50,760
[Caroline, echoing] I know how he can be.

1013
01:09:51,760 --> 01:09:53,120
But you know, Helene?

1014
01:09:53,800 --> 01:09:58,320
After you vanished,
I'd not known him devastated like that.

1015
01:09:59,560 --> 01:10:05,040
He loves you so much.
You and Alexander are everything to him.

1016
01:10:06,360 --> 01:10:09,720
[Helene] <i>Hi, I can't come to the phone</i>
<i>right now, please leave a message.</i>

1017
01:10:22,680 --> 01:10:24,680
[sounds distort]

1018
01:10:30,880 --> 01:10:32,680
[normality resumes]

1019
01:10:32,760 --> 01:10:34,040
[sighs]

1020
01:10:47,240 --> 01:10:48,400
[gasps]

1021
01:11:08,520 --> 01:11:10,880
[indistinct chatter echoes]

1022
01:11:10,960 --> 01:11:13,240
[distorted rumbling]

1023
01:11:16,520 --> 01:11:17,720
[indistinct chatter echoes]

1024
01:11:17,800 --> 01:11:19,720
[woman, echoes] Get away. I hate you!

1025
01:11:24,680 --> 01:11:25,920
Elisabeth?

1026
01:11:28,760 --> 01:11:30,760
[eerie music playing]

1027
01:11:50,840 --> 01:11:52,840
[music quickens]

1028
01:11:57,280 --> 01:11:59,320
[phone unlocks]

1029
01:12:02,840 --> 01:12:04,840
INBOX

1030
01:12:17,000 --> 01:12:18,600
I'VE TRIED CALLING YOU
SEVERAL TIMES.

1031
01:12:18,680 --> 01:12:20,440
IT'S IMPORTANT.
KIND REGARDS, ELISABETH

1032
01:12:22,760 --> 01:12:25,560
[Edmund breathes deeply]

1033
01:12:27,960 --> 01:12:28,960
Good morning.

1034
01:12:29,680 --> 01:12:30,800
Good morning.

1035
01:12:33,400 --> 01:12:34,960
-[Helene] Okay, so you go first.
-Mm.

1036
01:12:35,040 --> 01:12:37,600
-And no peeking. Mm.
-Uh-huh. Mm.

1037
01:12:38,800 --> 01:12:39,960
Coffee.

1038
01:12:40,040 --> 01:12:41,520
[Alexander humming happily]

1039
01:12:41,600 --> 01:12:44,360
[Edmund] I need to take a call,
and then we'll go.

1040
01:12:44,440 --> 01:12:45,480
It's your turn.

1041
01:12:45,960 --> 01:12:49,040
-Right, and so I draw… A body?
-A body. You start there.

1042
01:12:49,120 --> 01:12:50,080
[Helene] Okay.

1043
01:12:50,160 --> 01:12:51,960
[Edmund chattering on phone]

1044
01:12:52,040 --> 01:12:53,680
[Helene] Now it's your turn.

1045
01:12:53,760 --> 01:12:56,600
[Alexander humming happily]

1046
01:12:58,920 --> 01:13:00,920
[Edmund chattering indistinctly]

1047
01:13:11,640 --> 01:13:12,680
All finished.

1048
01:13:14,440 --> 01:13:15,400
Okay.

1049
01:13:15,480 --> 01:13:17,280
[children chattering]

1050
01:13:17,360 --> 01:13:19,240
[Helene] Have a great day. Mm.

1051
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:24,680
And hey you, I love you. You are my life.

1052
01:13:28,480 --> 01:13:29,480
What's wrong?

1053
01:13:30,120 --> 01:13:32,760
It's just that's what you said
before you went away.

1054
01:13:35,880 --> 01:13:39,640
Alexander, I won't leave you again, okay?

1055
01:13:40,320 --> 01:13:42,880
I'll never leave you again. I swear.

1056
01:13:43,480 --> 01:13:44,520
Never.

1057
01:13:45,360 --> 01:13:46,400
Come here.

1058
01:13:46,920 --> 01:13:49,520
-Mm. See you later.
-[Alexander] See ya.

1059
01:13:49,600 --> 01:13:50,920
-[bell ringing]
-Go on, then.

1060
01:13:51,000 --> 01:13:52,200
Yeah. Have fun.

1061
01:13:52,280 --> 01:13:53,360
[Alexander] Bye.

1062
01:13:54,240 --> 01:13:55,960
DYSSEGÅRD SCHOOL

1063
01:14:00,360 --> 01:14:02,920
[ominous electronic music playing]

1064
01:14:16,400 --> 01:14:17,600
[Edmund] What's he doing here?

1065
01:14:24,320 --> 01:14:26,200
[sighs] I don't want you talking
to him any more.

1066
01:14:26,280 --> 01:14:28,880
It might set you back
and I don't want you stressed.

1067
01:14:31,280 --> 01:14:32,760
I know.

1068
01:14:32,840 --> 01:14:36,120
But he won't go away
until I've said goodbye to him properly.

1069
01:14:36,200 --> 01:14:39,960
I promise I'll end things with him,
for the sake of our family.

1070
01:14:42,400 --> 01:14:43,400
Open it.

1071
01:14:47,320 --> 01:14:48,360
[lock clicks]

1072
01:15:00,360 --> 01:15:02,000
Hi. I've been trying to reach you.

1073
01:15:02,080 --> 01:15:04,880
I stopped by the house.
Did he speak to you about it?

1074
01:15:04,960 --> 01:15:07,760
-There's so much you need to see.
-Joachim.

1075
01:15:07,840 --> 01:15:10,080
-Joachim, stop. Stop it.
-I think he's hiding something--

1076
01:15:10,640 --> 01:15:13,000
We can't about it. Not here.

1077
01:15:13,080 --> 01:15:14,440
[Joachim] Are you scared of him?

1078
01:15:15,200 --> 01:15:16,360
Helene, if he's hurt you…

1079
01:15:16,440 --> 01:15:18,440
-I swear, I'm going to storm over…
-You can't. Stop.

1080
01:15:22,240 --> 01:15:23,920
He has to think I'm finishing it.

1081
01:15:26,000 --> 01:15:27,040
Okay?

1082
01:15:30,240 --> 01:15:31,440
Please trust me.

1083
01:15:36,560 --> 01:15:39,720
[Joachim] This is where I'm staying.
If you can make it there, we can talk.

1084
01:15:42,280 --> 01:15:43,320
-Yeah.
-[Joachim] Okay.

1085
01:15:43,960 --> 01:15:46,120
-[Helene] Vi må sige farvel nu.
-[Joachim] Okay.

1086
01:15:51,480 --> 01:15:56,120
You're right. Things don't add up.
But I'm figuring it out, okay?

1087
01:15:57,280 --> 01:15:58,520
I love you.

1088
01:16:00,920 --> 01:16:01,960
I love you.

1089
01:16:04,160 --> 01:16:06,600
[Helene breathing nervously]

1090
01:16:06,680 --> 01:16:07,720
[clears throat]

1091
01:16:26,720 --> 01:16:29,640
[indistinct chatter]

1092
01:16:33,360 --> 01:16:34,360
Yeah, okay.

1093
01:16:52,880 --> 01:16:57,240
[ominous electronic music playing]

1094
01:17:17,960 --> 01:17:19,960
Yes, see you tomorrow then. Take care.

1095
01:17:20,520 --> 01:17:24,680
Elisabeth, I need you to talk to me.
I'm not angry.

1096
01:17:24,760 --> 01:17:25,600
What?

1097
01:17:25,680 --> 01:17:28,480
Yeah, if you and Edmund are having
an affair and he dismissed you…

1098
01:17:28,560 --> 01:17:31,640
Look I have no idea what's going on,
but, um, I'm just looking for answers.

1099
01:17:31,720 --> 01:17:35,200
What are you talking about?
As if we're having an affair.

1100
01:17:36,720 --> 01:17:38,240
Then why won't you speak to me?

1101
01:17:38,320 --> 01:17:42,360
Because you lot forced me to sign a
legally-binding non-disclosure agreement!

1102
01:17:42,440 --> 01:17:46,560
Um. Wait, wait, stop, please.
Stop. Who did?

1103
01:17:47,200 --> 01:17:48,560
You know who did.

1104
01:17:49,400 --> 01:17:51,280
-Your husband.
-Hang on.

1105
01:17:53,080 --> 01:17:56,680
Okay. Um. Look, whatever…
I swear you can talk to me.

1106
01:17:56,760 --> 01:17:59,600
Yeah, I've heard it all before.
"You won't do anything."

1107
01:17:59,680 --> 01:18:01,400
I have no idea what you mean.

1108
01:18:01,480 --> 01:18:04,040
If we've talked already,
I don't remember it.

1109
01:18:05,320 --> 01:18:06,800
I don't remember it!

1110
01:18:10,960 --> 01:18:13,480
Just over two years ago, you contacted me.

1111
01:18:13,560 --> 01:18:15,560
And what I said then, is…

1112
01:18:16,400 --> 01:18:20,120
that I'd found out that one of our ships
was being used to commit crimes.

1113
01:18:20,640 --> 01:18:21,960
Serious stuff.

1114
01:18:22,040 --> 01:18:24,840
Buying women. Human trafficking.

1115
01:18:26,000 --> 01:18:27,760
Using your freight containers.

1116
01:18:28,960 --> 01:18:30,080
[sighs]

1117
01:18:34,240 --> 01:18:37,640
Okay. And how did you discover it?

1118
01:18:38,120 --> 01:18:41,880
I received emails from a woman
who said she had gathered some evidence.

1119
01:18:42,560 --> 01:18:44,840
You know, photos of the containers.

1120
01:18:45,520 --> 01:18:46,880
All the routes that were used.

1121
01:18:47,520 --> 01:18:48,600
Schedules.

1122
01:18:48,680 --> 01:18:50,840
She told me that it was systematic.

1123
01:18:50,920 --> 01:18:54,320
And it wouldn't be going on
if someone high up hadn't approved it.

1124
01:18:55,680 --> 01:18:59,720
She said she was working with the women
and she wanted to meet.

1125
01:19:00,720 --> 01:19:02,480
So she then gave me an address.

1126
01:19:02,560 --> 01:19:04,800
But before we could meet you contacted me.

1127
01:19:04,880 --> 01:19:07,200
You said
that you would take it from there.

1128
01:19:08,880 --> 01:19:10,160
Well, did we meet?

1129
01:19:10,240 --> 01:19:12,560
I don't know.
I never heard from you again.

1130
01:19:12,640 --> 01:19:15,080
And, well, I even thought that…

1131
01:19:16,320 --> 01:19:17,800
you were actually behind it.

1132
01:19:18,320 --> 01:19:19,640
It was a guess.

1133
01:19:20,240 --> 01:19:23,880
I tried to talk to Edmund.
I tried to contact him about it.

1134
01:19:23,960 --> 01:19:25,240
But he would just kill it.

1135
01:19:26,320 --> 01:19:28,000
Our contract was cancelled.

1136
01:19:28,680 --> 01:19:31,120
I was fired and forced to sign an NDA.

1137
01:19:32,080 --> 01:19:34,880
And I was even threatened
by one of Edmund's employees.

1138
01:19:35,600 --> 01:19:38,480
And I'm a single mum of two.
I couldn't risk it.

1139
01:19:38,560 --> 01:19:40,080
[Helene sighs]

1140
01:19:41,080 --> 01:19:43,000
That means they are still doing it.

1141
01:19:43,520 --> 01:19:45,280
Yes. I'd say you're right.

1142
01:19:46,200 --> 01:19:48,560
Do you still have her details
in your address book?

1143
01:19:48,640 --> 01:19:51,560
Yes. She told me to meet here.

1144
01:19:51,640 --> 01:19:53,960
-I think she worked there.
-Okay.

1145
01:19:54,480 --> 01:19:58,000
Promise me you'll be careful if
you're beginning to dig this all up again.

1146
01:19:58,080 --> 01:19:59,000
[Helene] I will.

1147
01:19:59,600 --> 01:20:02,160
And your contact, what was she called?

1148
01:20:02,240 --> 01:20:03,600
Louise.

1149
01:20:04,760 --> 01:20:05,920
Louise Andersen.

1150
01:20:06,000 --> 01:20:08,080
[intense music rises]

1151
01:20:10,440 --> 01:20:14,640
[electronic tense music playing]

1152
01:20:24,600 --> 01:20:27,040
NIGHTCLUB - GENTLEMENS CLUB

1153
01:20:28,720 --> 01:20:29,720
[lock clicks]

1154
01:20:33,120 --> 01:20:34,120
[dampened club music]

1155
01:20:34,200 --> 01:20:35,080
[woman] Hi.

1156
01:20:35,160 --> 01:20:36,080
[Helene] Hi there.

1157
01:20:36,760 --> 01:20:38,160
Can I help you?

1158
01:20:38,720 --> 01:20:40,120
I'm looking for Louise.

1159
01:20:42,440 --> 01:20:45,000
Sure, she won't be long. Go through.

1160
01:20:49,960 --> 01:20:55,320
["Something's Coming"
by The Regulators playing]

1161
01:21:01,360 --> 01:21:06,640
<i>♪ What was that tapping</i>
<i>On your window pane ♪</i>

1162
01:21:07,440 --> 01:21:12,640
<i>♪ Started in the distance</i>
<i>But no sign of rain ♪</i>

1163
01:21:14,120 --> 01:21:19,480
<i>♪ Shadows moving along the street ♪</i>

1164
01:21:20,080 --> 01:21:25,200
<i>♪ You feel your heart skip another beat… ♪</i>

1165
01:21:27,120 --> 01:21:29,320
-Louise?
-[Lulu] Close. My name's Lulu.

1166
01:21:30,160 --> 01:21:32,640
Do you want a drink? Champagne?

1167
01:21:32,720 --> 01:21:34,880
Uh, no.
I'm looking for a girl called Louise.

1168
01:21:34,960 --> 01:21:36,840
She worked here about two years ago.

1169
01:21:36,920 --> 01:21:38,080
Order the champagne.

1170
01:21:39,920 --> 01:21:41,720
Yeah. [clears throat] Okay.

1171
01:21:41,800 --> 01:21:44,000
A… A bottle of champagne, yeah.

1172
01:21:44,920 --> 01:21:47,600
<i>♪ And it's coming ♪</i>

1173
01:21:49,680 --> 01:21:52,600
<i>♪ It's coming for you ♪</i>

1174
01:21:52,680 --> 01:21:54,600
[distorted twinkling]

1175
01:21:54,680 --> 01:21:57,160
[indistinct voices echoing]

1176
01:22:00,440 --> 01:22:01,480
[champagne popping]

1177
01:22:01,560 --> 01:22:03,000
[classic rock music playing]

1178
01:22:05,120 --> 01:22:06,480
I hear you're looking for Louise?

1179
01:22:07,680 --> 01:22:08,800
Champagne.

1180
01:22:08,880 --> 01:22:11,320
Drink it.
Act like you're a normal customer.

1181
01:22:12,160 --> 01:22:13,800
-What do you want with her?
-[clears throat]

1182
01:22:14,280 --> 01:22:15,600
Did you know her?

1183
01:22:16,240 --> 01:22:17,200
Yeah.

1184
01:22:17,280 --> 01:22:18,720
We used to work together.

1185
01:22:18,800 --> 01:22:20,800
-Do you know where she is?
-No.

1186
01:22:20,880 --> 01:22:23,920
I haven't seen her in… Two, three years.

1187
01:22:26,280 --> 01:22:28,040
What happened to her?

1188
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:33,080
There was night after work
she told me she wasn't coming back here.

1189
01:22:33,760 --> 01:22:35,880
Well, did she tell you why that was?

1190
01:22:37,640 --> 01:22:38,760
She was afraid.

1191
01:22:39,480 --> 01:22:40,640
[customers laughing]

1192
01:22:40,720 --> 01:22:42,200
[Louise's colleague] I don't know why.

1193
01:22:44,120 --> 01:22:48,520
Did she ever mention that she knew girls
who had been trafficked here?

1194
01:22:49,280 --> 01:22:50,120
[scoffs]

1195
01:22:50,960 --> 01:22:54,120
All of us could say the same.
Most girls here at least.

1196
01:22:54,200 --> 01:22:56,240
-[champagne popping]
-[woman yelps]

1197
01:22:56,720 --> 01:22:58,720
[scattered laughter and cheering]

1198
01:23:04,040 --> 01:23:05,320
Can I give you some advice?

1199
01:23:06,520 --> 01:23:07,760
You should be cautious.

1200
01:23:07,840 --> 01:23:09,960
People who ask questions like that
end up in trouble.

1201
01:23:13,360 --> 01:23:14,720
Wait, one last question.

1202
01:23:14,800 --> 01:23:16,640
Do… Do you know where she went?

1203
01:23:16,720 --> 01:23:19,120
Mm, she told me
she was leaving the country.

1204
01:23:19,200 --> 01:23:20,600
Something about going to Norway.

1205
01:23:34,560 --> 01:23:36,560
[tense music playing]

1206
01:24:08,000 --> 01:24:09,440
[music intensifies]

1207
01:24:19,240 --> 01:24:21,960
[music becomes chaotic]

1208
01:24:32,800 --> 01:24:34,120
[music fades out]

1209
01:24:42,560 --> 01:24:43,560
[Helene breathing shakily]

1210
01:24:45,600 --> 01:24:46,560
[door handle rattling]

1211
01:24:52,720 --> 01:24:55,160
[door handle rattling]

1212
01:24:56,440 --> 01:24:58,440
[panicked breathing]

1213
01:25:21,200 --> 01:25:22,680
-[lock clicks open]
-[gasps softly]

1214
01:25:41,640 --> 01:25:42,480
[gaps]

1215
01:25:43,640 --> 01:25:45,640
[tense music playing]

1216
01:25:45,720 --> 01:25:46,800
[panting]

1217
01:25:46,880 --> 01:25:47,840
[Helene screaming]

1218
01:25:48,960 --> 01:25:51,560
[Helene] No! No! [straining]

1219
01:25:52,680 --> 01:25:54,280
[muffled screams]

1220
01:25:59,240 --> 01:26:01,240
[screaming subsides]

1221
01:26:13,600 --> 01:26:16,520
[mysterious music playing]

1222
01:26:25,920 --> 01:26:27,920
[doctor chats indistinctly]

1223
01:26:30,760 --> 01:26:32,280
[Edmund mutters indistinctly]

1224
01:26:35,480 --> 01:26:36,720
What?

1225
01:26:37,360 --> 01:26:38,400
Huh. You're awake.

1226
01:26:39,120 --> 01:26:40,120
Where am I?

1227
01:26:43,440 --> 01:26:45,880
Uh, slowly. Take it easy.

1228
01:26:46,680 --> 01:26:48,320
Yeah. Just relax.

1229
01:26:50,280 --> 01:26:53,480
[doctor] Helene, do you remember
how we discussed your medication?

1230
01:26:57,440 --> 01:26:58,400
Here you go.

1231
01:27:01,000 --> 01:27:02,240
You need to take two.

1232
01:27:04,720 --> 01:27:05,560
[læge] Mm.

1233
01:27:08,040 --> 01:27:09,040
Go ahead.

1234
01:27:11,080 --> 01:27:11,920
Mm.

1235
01:27:19,520 --> 01:27:21,200
Can I see? Open wide.

1236
01:27:23,800 --> 01:27:26,840
Helene, I've seen
every single trick in the book.

1237
01:27:40,520 --> 01:27:41,680
[doctor] Good.

1238
01:27:46,160 --> 01:27:47,800
[keypad beeping]

1239
01:27:51,560 --> 01:27:54,080
[electronic beeping]

1240
01:28:01,960 --> 01:28:03,760
[sighs] I had to.

1241
01:28:05,960 --> 01:28:07,520
I'm very sorry.

1242
01:28:08,960 --> 01:28:10,960
You just try and relax, okay?

1243
01:28:13,040 --> 01:28:13,920
[Edmund sighs]

1244
01:28:15,000 --> 01:28:16,760
Where's Alexander?

1245
01:28:16,840 --> 01:28:18,800
Well, he shouldn't see you like this.

1246
01:28:18,880 --> 01:28:19,760
[sighs]

1247
01:28:22,560 --> 01:28:23,920
What did you tell him?

1248
01:28:24,440 --> 01:28:26,480
[Edmund] I told him the truth.

1249
01:28:26,560 --> 01:28:28,800
I said that you're not well
and that you need rest.

1250
01:28:28,880 --> 01:28:29,760
He understood it.

1251
01:28:29,840 --> 01:28:31,280
-[scoffs]
-He's aware you're sick.

1252
01:28:32,680 --> 01:28:33,720
[shuddering]

1253
01:28:35,280 --> 01:28:37,520
I… I want to go home now.

1254
01:28:37,600 --> 01:28:40,080
-I want to go home to Alexander.
-I understand.

1255
01:28:40,960 --> 01:28:42,160
And we can do that.

1256
01:28:42,240 --> 01:28:44,760
But there's paperwork to deal with first.

1257
01:28:51,680 --> 01:28:53,680
APPOINTMENT OF GUARDIANSHIP

1258
01:28:53,760 --> 01:28:54,960
[Helene scoffs]

1259
01:28:56,720 --> 01:28:59,120
You… You want me under guardianship?

1260
01:29:00,120 --> 01:29:01,560
I'm trying to help.

1261
01:29:02,800 --> 01:29:04,760
I want you to have the best possible care.

1262
01:29:04,840 --> 01:29:05,680
[Helene scoffs]

1263
01:29:06,520 --> 01:29:07,360
[Edmund sighs]

1264
01:29:13,480 --> 01:29:16,560
Helene… I don't think you're listening.

1265
01:29:18,440 --> 01:29:20,800
This is for your own wellbeing. Hmm?

1266
01:29:24,680 --> 01:29:26,360
You can't run away again.

1267
01:29:29,160 --> 01:29:30,720
I know
what my father was trying to tell me.

1268
01:29:30,800 --> 01:29:31,760
[sighs]

1269
01:29:32,520 --> 01:29:34,200
[Helene] And I know who Louise is.

1270
01:29:36,480 --> 01:29:39,080
-You won't get away with this, Edmund.
-Oh, my love… [exhales]

1271
01:29:42,000 --> 01:29:46,680
You're seeing things you've imagined.
Things that aren't even real.

1272
01:29:52,600 --> 01:29:57,920
The pills will kick in soon. I've packed
some things for you to last a few days.

1273
01:29:58,800 --> 01:30:00,360
Try to get some rest.

1274
01:30:00,440 --> 01:30:03,520
I'll leave the papers here.
You can sign them when you feel better.

1275
01:30:05,200 --> 01:30:06,640
[sighs]

1276
01:30:10,800 --> 01:30:12,080
I love you.

1277
01:30:12,160 --> 01:30:14,520
[ominous music playing]

1278
01:30:14,600 --> 01:30:17,040
Soon you'll be your old self again.

1279
01:30:24,680 --> 01:30:26,680
[keypad beeping]

1280
01:30:53,640 --> 01:30:54,480
[dampened] Hello!

1281
01:30:57,080 --> 01:30:58,440
Hello!

1282
01:30:59,240 --> 01:31:01,560
Let me out! I need to see my son!

1283
01:31:21,680 --> 01:31:24,120
[retching]

1284
01:31:40,240 --> 01:31:42,160
[distorted twinkling]

1285
01:31:42,240 --> 01:31:43,920
[panting]

1286
01:31:45,960 --> 01:31:47,720
[suspenseful music playing]

1287
01:31:58,440 --> 01:31:59,840
We tried to escape.

1288
01:32:02,040 --> 01:32:03,160
[Louise echoes] <i>Helene!</i>

1289
01:32:06,720 --> 01:32:10,040
Helene! [panting] He's found us.

1290
01:32:10,120 --> 01:32:11,160
[foghorn blaring]

1291
01:32:11,240 --> 01:32:12,600
[Helene] There's a ship

1292
01:32:14,440 --> 01:32:16,200
I think we can make it if we jump.

1293
01:32:16,280 --> 01:32:18,920
What, have you gone crazy?
We can't do that.

1294
01:32:22,280 --> 01:32:24,720
[music intensifies]

1295
01:32:34,600 --> 01:32:35,640
Damn it!

1296
01:32:51,480 --> 01:32:54,640
[alarm ringing]

1297
01:32:59,880 --> 01:33:02,120
[alarm intensifies]

1298
01:33:02,880 --> 01:33:05,200
[Peter] Ah! Come here!

1299
01:33:05,280 --> 01:33:07,560
-[Helene straining]
-[Peter grunts]

1300
01:33:07,640 --> 01:33:09,040
[panting]

1301
01:33:15,160 --> 01:33:17,320
[Peter coughing]

1302
01:33:18,400 --> 01:33:19,880
[persistent knocking]

1303
01:33:22,560 --> 01:33:24,640
[knocking continues]

1304
01:33:29,920 --> 01:33:32,480
[Helene panting]

1305
01:33:33,960 --> 01:33:37,520
They're looking for me.
Is there any way they'd know this address?

1306
01:33:37,600 --> 01:33:39,440
-No, no, no.
-[Helene] Okay.

1307
01:33:40,800 --> 01:33:42,160
He has Alexander.

1308
01:33:43,240 --> 01:33:45,560
-I won't leave him there.
-[Joachim] We'll figure it out.

1309
01:33:46,280 --> 01:33:49,400
[Helene] I knew her.
Louise Andersen. I met her.

1310
01:33:49,480 --> 01:33:50,320
Okay?

1311
01:33:50,400 --> 01:33:52,480
I was in contact with her, and she…

1312
01:33:52,960 --> 01:33:54,000
had evidence.

1313
01:33:54,080 --> 01:33:56,240
Proof that Edmund was using the company
for trafficking.

1314
01:33:56,320 --> 01:33:58,880
All right. Uh, tell me the whole story.

1315
01:34:00,880 --> 01:34:02,400
She fled to Norway. Um…

1316
01:34:02,480 --> 01:34:05,440
-Louise?
-Yes. And I followed her, and…

1317
01:34:07,320 --> 01:34:09,200
We… We were on a bridge, and I…

1318
01:34:09,280 --> 01:34:10,800
There was a bridge?

1319
01:34:11,440 --> 01:34:13,600
[Joachim] Where is it? Oh… damn.

1320
01:34:17,240 --> 01:34:18,280
Er det den?

1321
01:34:20,960 --> 01:34:24,040
I've been thinking a lot about that ship
and trying to figure out

1322
01:34:24,120 --> 01:34:26,240
how you got onto it if you didn't board
as a passenger,

1323
01:34:26,320 --> 01:34:28,120
and it's crazy, but what if you jumped?

1324
01:34:29,480 --> 01:34:33,280
And if you take the ship routes
and heights into account…

1325
01:34:33,760 --> 01:34:35,960
then this was the only place.

1326
01:34:36,040 --> 01:34:38,360
[Helene] <i>Give me your bag and run.</i>

1327
01:34:38,440 --> 01:34:39,880
I'll stop him and speak to him.

1328
01:34:39,960 --> 01:34:42,640
-You can't! No way!
-You've done enough.

1329
01:34:42,720 --> 01:34:44,200
[Helene] Give me your bag.

1330
01:34:49,480 --> 01:34:51,840
Run. Go!

1331
01:34:54,520 --> 01:34:57,160
[suspenseful music playing]

1332
01:34:58,240 --> 01:34:59,200
[Helene] Stop!

1333
01:35:01,960 --> 01:35:02,880
Stop!

1334
01:35:04,320 --> 01:35:05,440
[exclaims erratically]

1335
01:35:05,520 --> 01:35:07,080
-[Louise screaming]
-[gasps]

1336
01:35:21,560 --> 01:35:23,320
[foghorn blaring]

1337
01:35:26,080 --> 01:35:27,000
[music intensifies]

1338
01:35:30,240 --> 01:35:31,840
-[Helene strains]
-[Edmund] Helene!

1339
01:35:36,240 --> 01:35:37,080
Helene…

1340
01:35:37,160 --> 01:35:38,840
[panting]

1341
01:35:42,440 --> 01:35:43,400
Don't do it.

1342
01:35:45,520 --> 01:35:47,520
[trembling]

1343
01:35:52,760 --> 01:35:53,760
[Edmund] Helene…

1344
01:35:54,440 --> 01:35:57,200
I beg you. Don't do it.

1345
01:35:57,280 --> 01:36:00,320
[music intensifies, halts]

1346
01:36:03,480 --> 01:36:04,560
It was Edmund.

1347
01:36:05,600 --> 01:36:11,200
He… He killed Louise.
And I saw it and then I… I jumped.

1348
01:36:18,320 --> 01:36:19,680
She gave me a…

1349
01:36:35,080 --> 01:36:37,080
-Look at that…
-[gasps]

1350
01:36:41,720 --> 01:36:42,760
[laughs softly]

1351
01:36:43,280 --> 01:36:46,040
-I kept it hidden.
-[Joachim] A little too hidden.

1352
01:36:48,080 --> 01:36:49,360
[doorbell ringing]

1353
01:36:51,880 --> 01:36:52,720
Hi.

1354
01:36:52,800 --> 01:36:56,200
-Helene?
-[Helene] I need your help.

1355
01:36:58,840 --> 01:37:00,200
Found it.

1356
01:37:02,320 --> 01:37:04,200
What do we think we'll find on it?

1357
01:37:04,280 --> 01:37:05,360
[clears throat]

1358
01:37:05,440 --> 01:37:06,720
Beviser af en slags.

1359
01:37:07,440 --> 01:37:09,440
[inhales, exhales]

1360
01:37:20,600 --> 01:37:24,040
My goodness. What is it?

1361
01:37:26,400 --> 01:37:27,440
Trafficking.

1362
01:37:33,080 --> 01:37:35,320
[inhales sharply] In our containers?

1363
01:37:35,400 --> 01:37:37,680
Yes. Edmund used my father's business.

1364
01:37:37,760 --> 01:37:40,360
So everything
that Elisabeth said was right.

1365
01:37:40,440 --> 01:37:41,480
[Helene] Yes.

1366
01:37:41,560 --> 01:37:44,120
And then Edmund tried bury the evidence

1367
01:37:47,680 --> 01:37:49,320
-[Ingrid] No.
-Hvad er der?

1368
01:37:49,840 --> 01:37:51,040
That ship…

1369
01:37:51,880 --> 01:37:54,080
[Ingrid] We've been working with
the firm that owns that ship

1370
01:37:54,160 --> 01:37:55,720
for a long time.

1371
01:37:55,800 --> 01:37:57,840
From before Edmund joined the company.

1372
01:37:58,560 --> 01:37:59,440
Since when?

1373
01:38:07,680 --> 01:38:08,960
[Ingrid] Over 50 years.

1374
01:38:15,000 --> 01:38:17,560
Weren't these the pages
that were torn from my book?

1375
01:38:17,640 --> 01:38:18,960
Uh, yes, I think so.

1376
01:38:24,000 --> 01:38:25,880
[Ingrid] Helene, I have to tell you…

1377
01:38:26,480 --> 01:38:27,920
JM Shipping…

1378
01:38:28,000 --> 01:38:30,680
These were some of our partnerships
that your father handled.

1379
01:38:30,760 --> 01:38:33,000
He didn't want me to get involved in it.

1380
01:38:33,080 --> 01:38:35,560
[distorted rumbling]

1381
01:38:38,120 --> 01:38:39,360
CO-OPERATION FOR LIFE

1382
01:38:39,440 --> 01:38:40,440
{\an8}AKSEL SÖDERBERG
WITH J. M. SHIPPING

1383
01:38:44,400 --> 01:38:48,160
[Ingrid] Edmund is probably involved
as well. It all points to that, but…

1384
01:38:48,920 --> 01:38:52,920
I'd say it started long before
he joined the firm, and there's no doubt.

1385
01:38:53,000 --> 01:38:56,040
So, my father started it?

1386
01:38:57,600 --> 01:38:58,640
Yeah.

1387
01:39:01,040 --> 01:39:03,080
So that's what he was trying to say…

1388
01:39:03,160 --> 01:39:06,120
Before he died,
he tried to confess, and warn me.

1389
01:39:06,200 --> 01:39:07,600
[Aksel] Edmund…

1390
01:39:14,800 --> 01:39:16,400
So, what now?

1391
01:39:16,480 --> 01:39:19,960
-I need to get Alexander.
-

1392
01:39:20,040 --> 01:39:21,680
I must confront Edmund.

1393
01:39:21,760 --> 01:39:23,120
Yes, but Edmund is evil.

1394
01:39:23,200 --> 01:39:24,840
There's nothing he can do!
I have evidence.

1395
01:39:24,920 --> 01:39:28,120
So take that evidence to the police
so we can get out of this.

1396
01:39:28,200 --> 01:39:31,280
But we can't wait
for the police to look at it, Joachim.

1397
01:39:31,360 --> 01:39:33,400
They'll take months,
and he has a million lawyers,

1398
01:39:33,480 --> 01:39:35,600
and he can talk his way out of everything.

1399
01:39:36,240 --> 01:39:40,000
And yes, he is evil.
That's why I have to rescue Alexander.

1400
01:39:42,000 --> 01:39:45,440
[Caroline] "Should I leave the road
or go into the woods alone

1401
01:39:46,280 --> 01:39:48,400
when my mother has forbidden it."

1402
01:39:48,480 --> 01:39:50,040
[classical music playing]

1403
01:39:50,120 --> 01:39:51,960
-Mm?
-[Alexander] Grandma?

1404
01:39:52,040 --> 01:39:54,680
-Mm?
-Is Mum coming home?

1405
01:39:55,840 --> 01:39:58,160
Yes, I'm sure she'll soon be home again.

1406
01:40:00,680 --> 01:40:05,240
Don't you worry, darling.
Sleep tight. Good night.

1407
01:40:06,200 --> 01:40:07,960
-[Caroline] Goodnight.
-[Alexander] Goodnight.

1408
01:40:19,320 --> 01:40:21,160
She'll come home again.

1409
01:40:22,880 --> 01:40:23,920
Okay.

1410
01:40:25,680 --> 01:40:27,040
[Caroline] I'm going to bed.

1411
01:40:27,640 --> 01:40:29,640
[electronic suspenseful music playing]

1412
01:40:57,640 --> 01:41:00,480
Come and find me
if I'm not back in ten minutes.

1413
01:41:01,600 --> 01:41:02,680
Be safe.

1414
01:41:18,760 --> 01:41:22,920
Great to have you home again.
Would you like some wine?

1415
01:41:25,040 --> 01:41:27,880
I know what you and my father were doing.

1416
01:41:29,600 --> 01:41:31,080
I have proof now.

1417
01:41:31,680 --> 01:41:33,240
It's hidden in a safe place.

1418
01:41:34,760 --> 01:41:38,760
Alexander comes with me.
Let us go, and it stays hidden.

1419
01:41:41,000 --> 01:41:43,360
But we are leaving you.
And you have to let us.

1420
01:41:43,440 --> 01:41:47,400
Helene, you do not have a clue
what this is about.

1421
01:41:48,800 --> 01:41:51,920
[Edmund sighs] I can't let you go.

1422
01:41:53,000 --> 01:41:57,440
In fact, I won't allow you
to disappear again.

1423
01:41:59,600 --> 01:42:00,760
Allow me to?

1424
01:42:04,800 --> 01:42:06,320
You let me disappear.

1425
01:42:07,320 --> 01:42:09,680
And you ensured that they found me again.

1426
01:42:10,200 --> 01:42:11,160
Okay.

1427
01:42:16,240 --> 01:42:20,760
It might be for the best if I explain
exactly what happened…

1428
01:42:22,280 --> 01:42:24,880
But afterwards,
I think you'll want to stay with me.

1429
01:42:26,160 --> 01:42:27,480
[inhales] You're right.

1430
01:42:28,640 --> 01:42:31,520
[Edmund] You discovered
the company's involvement in trafficking

1431
01:42:32,080 --> 01:42:33,560
two years ago.

1432
01:42:33,640 --> 01:42:36,960
I wanted to stop you.
However, I couldn't stop you in time.

1433
01:42:37,720 --> 01:42:39,000
You got away.

1434
01:42:39,560 --> 01:42:43,320
At first, I thought you'd died in Norway.

1435
01:42:45,120 --> 01:42:48,600
But then I discovered
you started an entirely new life.

1436
01:42:49,520 --> 01:42:52,960
I had a hard time believing
the story about amnesia.

1437
01:42:54,440 --> 01:42:56,680
[sighs] But in the end it was true.
Or was it?

1438
01:42:57,280 --> 01:42:58,320
Or was it?

1439
01:42:59,160 --> 01:43:00,560
Were you watching me?

1440
01:43:01,160 --> 01:43:02,760
[Edmund chuckles softly] Yeah.

1441
01:43:04,800 --> 01:43:06,280
Of course I was.

1442
01:43:07,440 --> 01:43:09,440
It became almost like an obsession.

1443
01:43:12,000 --> 01:43:13,840
And yet it really pained me…

1444
01:43:14,840 --> 01:43:15,920
to see you…

1445
01:43:16,680 --> 01:43:17,800
with him.

1446
01:43:20,920 --> 01:43:22,600
[ominous music playing]

1447
01:43:36,080 --> 01:43:39,880
[Edmund] It wasn't easy for me
to see you living a life without me.

1448
01:43:39,960 --> 01:43:41,280
But I handled it.

1449
01:43:42,680 --> 01:43:44,640
Well, until it got too much for me.

1450
01:43:44,720 --> 01:43:48,200
I couldn't take seeing you
engaged to another man.

1451
01:43:48,280 --> 01:43:50,400
So I had to bring you home again.

1452
01:43:53,080 --> 01:43:54,400
Helene…

1453
01:43:58,200 --> 01:43:59,280
You're mine.

1454
01:44:02,440 --> 01:44:03,560
[knives slinking]

1455
01:44:05,680 --> 01:44:07,000
We belong together.

1456
01:44:07,080 --> 01:44:09,080
[breathing nervously]

1457
01:44:15,880 --> 01:44:18,400
[Edmund]I knew that bringing you home
was a big risk.

1458
01:44:18,480 --> 01:44:21,440
It was a gamble to trust that
you wouldn't regain your memories,

1459
01:44:21,520 --> 01:44:23,960
which was, of course, naive.

1460
01:44:26,000 --> 01:44:29,320
You let our son live
without his mother for two years.

1461
01:44:31,920 --> 01:44:33,920
But I did let you live, Helene.

1462
01:44:35,080 --> 01:44:36,040
[inhales sharply]

1463
01:44:49,560 --> 01:44:51,640
What about Louise?
You didn't let her live.

1464
01:44:51,720 --> 01:44:53,440
-No.
-You killed her.

1465
01:44:54,600 --> 01:44:57,720
-She was ruining what we had.
-[scoffs] You're insane.

1466
01:45:01,080 --> 01:45:02,160
I love you.

1467
01:45:03,680 --> 01:45:06,320
I love you more than anything
in this world.

1468
01:45:06,400 --> 01:45:08,800
[grunts] I'm going to get Alexander.

1469
01:45:09,880 --> 01:45:11,480
And you'll let us go.

1470
01:45:12,120 --> 01:45:13,880
-No.
-[Helene] Yes, you will.

1471
01:45:13,960 --> 01:45:16,280
-No.
-You're going to, I have evidence!

1472
01:45:16,360 --> 01:45:18,760
The proof you have
mainly implicates your father,

1473
01:45:18,840 --> 01:45:20,360
and he's not here to contest it.

1474
01:45:21,000 --> 01:45:23,880
So then who takes the fall? Our company.

1475
01:45:24,560 --> 01:45:28,040
And our company, my love…
That's you and me.

1476
01:45:28,600 --> 01:45:30,600
Hi, Ingrid.
I wanted to ask you about something.

1477
01:45:30,680 --> 01:45:33,600
That book you showed us
with old employees?

1478
01:45:33,680 --> 01:45:36,720
-[Ingrid] <i>yes?</i>
-In the photo from 1976.

1479
01:45:36,800 --> 01:45:40,640
There's a tall blonde lady in the line.
She looks familiar.

1480
01:45:40,720 --> 01:45:43,920
If you go to the police,
I'll take you down with me.

1481
01:45:44,000 --> 01:45:46,800
So how about we just sort this out
as a family?

1482
01:45:46,880 --> 01:45:49,640
-Don't come near me.
-Don't shout, you'll wake Alexander up.

1483
01:45:49,720 --> 01:45:53,240
<i>The woman on the left.</i>
<i>That's Caroline, Edmund's mother.</i>

1484
01:45:54,600 --> 01:45:56,280
Mother, can you sort her out?

1485
01:45:56,840 --> 01:45:58,640
[Helene choking]

1486
01:46:01,480 --> 01:46:02,800
[Helene falls to the floor]

1487
01:46:04,680 --> 01:46:06,640
And did she work at the company?

1488
01:46:06,720 --> 01:46:10,160
<i>Yes. She was Aksel Söderberg's secretary</i>
<i>before me.</i>

1489
01:46:12,120 --> 01:46:14,120
[electronic suspenseful music playing]

1490
01:46:19,480 --> 01:46:21,480
[Helene breathing heavily]

1491
01:46:26,080 --> 01:46:27,400
[woman] You can't treat me like this!

1492
01:46:27,480 --> 01:46:29,320
[Aksel] Come back !
Don't you walk away from me!

1493
01:46:29,400 --> 01:46:32,400
-Get off me! Get away! I hate you!
-[Aksel] Hey! Wait!

1494
01:46:33,200 --> 01:46:35,360
This is what happens
when you treat me like this.

1495
01:46:35,440 --> 01:46:37,440
Stop this. Caroline!

1496
01:46:40,880 --> 01:46:42,320
[Helene slurs] It was you.

1497
01:46:44,000 --> 01:46:46,040
You were here, when I was little.

1498
01:46:46,120 --> 01:46:48,280
Get her upstairs or she'll wake Alexander.

1499
01:46:56,160 --> 01:46:58,200
-[Helene moaning softly]
-[Caroline] Put her on the bed.

1500
01:46:58,280 --> 01:47:00,280
-Let go.
-Easy.

1501
01:47:00,360 --> 01:47:02,680
-[panicked breathing]
-[Edmund] Easy, easy, easy.

1502
01:47:04,440 --> 01:47:07,120
Okay. Okay.

1503
01:47:07,720 --> 01:47:11,120
Why were you here back then?
You said you didn't know my father well.

1504
01:47:11,200 --> 01:47:14,200
Helene, your father was a bad man.

1505
01:47:15,560 --> 01:47:16,640
What are you talking about?

1506
01:47:16,720 --> 01:47:18,720
For eight years, I looked after him.

1507
01:47:20,000 --> 01:47:22,000
I loved him. Worshipped him.

1508
01:47:22,600 --> 01:47:24,200
He said he loved me as well.

1509
01:47:25,040 --> 01:47:26,760
He promised we'd get married.

1510
01:47:27,320 --> 01:47:29,040
But as soon as he met your mother,

1511
01:47:29,120 --> 01:47:32,640
he broke it off with me for her.
He cast me out.

1512
01:47:33,400 --> 01:47:34,920
I wasn't good enough any longer.

1513
01:47:35,000 --> 01:47:38,880
-[dispatcher] <i>What's your emergency?</i>
<i>-</i>Hi. I think I need some help here.

1514
01:47:38,960 --> 01:47:41,800
<i>-What's your location?</i>
-Could you send the police to, uh…

1515
01:47:42,440 --> 01:47:44,080
-Lindevej 12.
<i>-Yes, of course.</i>

1516
01:47:44,160 --> 01:47:45,960
<i>Can you tell me what this is about?</i>

1517
01:47:46,480 --> 01:47:49,440
[Peter and Joachim grunting]

1518
01:47:57,080 --> 01:48:01,960
He underestimated mother
and how much she knew about his secrets.

1519
01:48:02,680 --> 01:48:06,120
I had to make sure
Edmund had a future at Söderberg

1520
01:48:06,800 --> 01:48:08,120
We deserved it.

1521
01:48:08,200 --> 01:48:11,520
So I forced Aksel to hire Edmund.

1522
01:48:11,600 --> 01:48:15,160
But Helene, you have to believe me.
Our love…

1523
01:48:16,360 --> 01:48:17,840
It was always real.

1524
01:48:18,680 --> 01:48:20,680
[both grunting]

1525
01:48:29,600 --> 01:48:31,360
You two are sick.

1526
01:48:31,440 --> 01:48:33,520
You see? I told you she'd react this way.

1527
01:48:33,600 --> 01:48:34,840
She just needs a bit more time.

1528
01:48:34,920 --> 01:48:37,680
Last time you let her live
you saw what happened!

1529
01:48:38,200 --> 01:48:40,480
You know she has to die,
just like her father.

1530
01:48:41,080 --> 01:48:43,640
So that everything
we've fought for isn't ruined.

1531
01:48:44,880 --> 01:48:48,640
Dad? [panting] Dad? Dad? Dad?

1532
01:48:53,080 --> 01:48:56,640
[panting] You killed my father
to stop him confessing?

1533
01:48:56,720 --> 01:49:00,600
Remarkable how you find your morality
when close to death, wouldn't you say?

1534
01:49:02,000 --> 01:49:03,800
[both grunting]

1535
01:49:11,640 --> 01:49:13,040
You're going to have to finish it.

1536
01:49:13,680 --> 01:49:16,120
-I'll get her to come around.
-[Caroline] No, Edmund!

1537
01:49:16,200 --> 01:49:20,880
You insisted on bringing Helene home
and I let you, but it didn't work, okay?

1538
01:49:20,960 --> 01:49:22,000
So this stops here!

1539
01:49:22,080 --> 01:49:23,280
[Edmund] Mother!

1540
01:49:23,360 --> 01:49:25,360
[Helene breathing shakily]

1541
01:49:28,120 --> 01:49:29,720
It is my decision.

1542
01:49:29,800 --> 01:49:31,600
[inhales angrily] You're pathetic.

1543
01:49:32,280 --> 01:49:35,040
This is pathetic. She doesn't want you,
don't you see that?

1544
01:49:35,680 --> 01:49:37,280
Don't you see that?

1545
01:49:39,720 --> 01:49:40,960
Fine, I'll do it.

1546
01:49:41,880 --> 01:49:42,760
[Helene struggling]

1547
01:49:42,840 --> 01:49:46,280
Stop! Stop! Mother, stop it! Stop it now!

1548
01:49:46,760 --> 01:49:48,160
Stop! Stop, hey!

1549
01:49:48,240 --> 01:49:50,320
She's still Alexander's mother!

1550
01:49:50,920 --> 01:49:51,960
[Edmund grunts]

1551
01:49:53,480 --> 01:49:55,080
-No!
-[Caroline screams]

1552
01:49:55,520 --> 01:49:56,520
-[body thuds]
-[gaps]

1553
01:49:57,080 --> 01:49:58,560
No. No…

1554
01:49:59,640 --> 01:50:01,240
[panting]

1555
01:50:02,320 --> 01:50:04,400
Mother… Mother…

1556
01:50:05,400 --> 01:50:07,880
Mother… Mother…

1557
01:50:10,880 --> 01:50:12,920
[Edmund] No. No.

1558
01:50:13,760 --> 01:50:15,080
[sighs]

1559
01:50:16,200 --> 01:50:18,880
[breathing heavily]

1560
01:50:30,640 --> 01:50:33,320
[tense music rises]

1561
01:50:34,720 --> 01:50:36,720
[music steadies]

1562
01:50:41,400 --> 01:50:44,520
-[door thuds]
-[Edmund] Mother! Mother!

1563
01:50:46,800 --> 01:50:50,640
[softly] Mother… No. No.

1564
01:50:50,760 --> 01:50:52,760
[sobbing]

1565
01:50:56,320 --> 01:50:58,320
[sirens whirring]

1566
01:51:02,320 --> 01:51:04,320
[mysterious music playing]

1567
01:51:06,880 --> 01:51:08,680
[indistinct police radio]

1568
01:51:16,720 --> 01:51:18,720
[mysterious music swells]

1569
01:51:39,720 --> 01:51:41,160
[music steadies, softens]

1570
01:52:12,680 --> 01:52:15,320
[police officer over radio] <i>Traffic police</i>
<i>have been notified.</i>

1571
01:52:15,400 --> 01:52:18,840
<i>An ambulance is on the way</i>
<i>to the crime scene, ETA 20 minutes.</i>

1572
01:52:18,920 --> 01:52:20,920
[radio continues indistinctly]

1573
01:52:23,960 --> 01:52:28,280
[bright music playing]

1574
01:52:30,160 --> 01:52:31,000
Yes, it is!

1575
01:52:33,120 --> 01:52:35,680
You see? See that white house there?

1576
01:52:35,760 --> 01:52:38,680
-Yeah.
-With the swimming pier? You see it?

1577
01:52:38,760 --> 01:52:40,080
Will we live there?

1578
01:52:40,160 --> 01:52:41,720
[Helene] If you'd like to.

1579
01:52:43,600 --> 01:52:45,280
-[Alexander] Come on, Mummy!
-[Helene] Whoo!

1580
01:52:45,360 --> 01:52:47,720
-[Joachim] Here she comes!
-[Alexander] Yeah.

1581
01:52:47,800 --> 01:52:49,200
[Helene] Oh, it's cold!

1582
01:52:50,200 --> 01:52:51,800
[boys chattering indistinctly]

1583
01:52:51,880 --> 01:52:54,240
-[Joachim] I'm gonna spin you. Go on.
-[Alexander] All right.

1584
01:52:54,320 --> 01:52:56,320
-[Alexander chuckles]
-Here we go!

1585
01:52:56,400 --> 01:52:58,120
[both chuckle]

1586
01:52:58,200 --> 01:53:00,520
-Ah!
-[both chuckle]

1587
01:53:00,600 --> 01:53:02,480
[Alexander] Okay, again! Come on!

1588
01:53:02,560 --> 01:53:05,080
[Joachim] Throw it to me over there
and then I'll swim over.

1589
01:53:05,160 --> 01:53:06,800
[Alexander] Great. You gonna swim under?

1590
01:53:06,880 --> 01:53:10,360
[Joachim] Yeah I'll swim under,
and then I'll come back to you, okay?

1591
01:53:10,440 --> 01:53:11,440
Throw it to me.

1592
01:53:11,520 --> 01:53:13,440
-[Alexander] Oh!
-[Joachim] Okay, are you ready?

1593
01:53:13,520 --> 01:53:14,400
[Alexander] Yeah.

1594
01:53:14,480 --> 01:53:17,000
-[Joachim] Okay. Three, two, one. Throw!
-[Alexander grunts]

1595
01:53:17,640 --> 01:53:19,360
[Joachim laughs] No, further than that!

1596
01:53:19,440 --> 01:53:21,720
Hey, Mum, it's really great here!

1597
01:53:22,960 --> 01:53:25,520
[exhales] You always did like swimming.

1598
01:53:26,560 --> 01:53:28,320
Can you remember now?

1599
01:53:28,920 --> 01:53:30,480
[Helene] A few things, yes.

1600
01:53:34,160 --> 01:53:35,760
[dramatic flourish]

1601
01:53:36,680 --> 01:53:39,440
{\an8}["Running Away" by Hoffman,
Estrada og Franklin playing]